[{"id":"a006","title":"絕緣層上覆矽晶圓製造","titleEn":"Silicon-on-insulator wafer fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["SOI 結構分工","鍵合與層轉移","薄層量測","元件相容性"],"labelsEn":["SOI layer functions","Bonding and layer transfer","Thin-layer measurements","Device compatibility"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a006-stage01","order":1,"title":"SOI 結構分工","titleEn":"SOI layer functions","description":"在「SOI 結構分工」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for soi layer functions, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a006-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"辨認三層結構","titleEn":"Identify the three-layer stack","objective":"完成「辨認三層結構」的因果圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for identify the three-layer stack, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：辨認三層結構。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify the three-layer stack. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「辨認三層結構」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify the three-layer stack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「辨認三層結構」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for identify the three-layer stack: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-01-k1","title":"辨認三層結構的原理","titleEn":"Identify the three-layer stack principle","text":"頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。","textEn":"Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles."},{"id":"a006-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「辨認三層結構」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify the three-layer stack?","options":["頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。","TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles.","TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"頂矽、埋氧與支撐晶圓分別承擔不同功能。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Top silicon, buried oxide and handle wafer have different roles. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-01"],"title":"選擇層轉移路徑","titleEn":"Compare layer-transfer routes","objective":"完成「選擇層轉移路徑」的對照表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare layer-transfer routes, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：選擇層轉移路徑。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare layer-transfer routes. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「選擇層轉移路徑」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare layer-transfer routes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「選擇層轉移路徑」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare layer-transfer routes: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-02-k1","title":"選擇層轉移路徑的原理","titleEn":"Compare layer-transfer routes principle","text":"鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。","textEn":"Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms."},{"id":"a006-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「選擇層轉移路徑」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare layer-transfer routes?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鍵合後研薄與離子切割不是同一轉移機制。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Bond-and-thin and ion-cut use different transfer mechanisms. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-02"],"title":"頂矽厚度預算","titleEn":"Budget top-silicon thickness","objective":"完成「頂矽厚度預算」的敏感度草圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for budget top-silicon thickness, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：頂矽厚度預算。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂厚度帳：頂矽轉移後 120 個任意厚度單位、修整消耗 15、後續氧化消耗矽 5；求剩餘量，再檢查是否有把氧化物厚度誤當成矽消耗。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget top-silicon thickness. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical thickness ledger: transferred top silicon 120 arbitrary units, finishing consumes 15 and later oxidation consumes 5 silicon units. Compute the remainder and check that oxide thickness was not confused with silicon consumption.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「頂矽厚度預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget top-silicon thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「頂矽厚度預算」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for budget top-silicon thickness: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-03-k1","title":"頂矽厚度預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget top-silicon thickness principle","text":"分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。","textEn":"Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance."},{"id":"a006-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「頂矽厚度預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget top-silicon thickness?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。","分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry.","Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分裂後修整會消耗頂矽留量。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Post-split finishing consumes top-silicon allowance. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-03"],"title":"埋氧厚度作用","titleEn":"Assess buried-oxide thickness","objective":"完成「埋氧厚度作用」的故障判別表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess buried-oxide thickness, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：埋氧厚度作用。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess buried-oxide thickness. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「埋氧厚度作用」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess buried-oxide thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「埋氧厚度作用」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess buried-oxide thickness: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-04-k1","title":"埋氧厚度作用的原理","titleEn":"Assess buried-oxide thickness principle","text":"埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。","textEn":"Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow."},{"id":"a006-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「埋氧厚度作用」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess buried-oxide thickness?","options":["埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。","TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow.","TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"埋氧同時影響電隔離與熱傳。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Buried oxide affects electrical isolation and heat flow. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-04"],"title":"供體可回收性","titleEn":"Plan donor reuse","objective":"完成「供體可回收性」的量測規劃，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for plan donor reuse, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：供體可回收性。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Plan donor reuse. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「供體可回收性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for plan donor reuse and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「供體可回收性」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for plan donor reuse: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-05-k1","title":"供體可回收性的原理","titleEn":"Plan donor reuse principle","text":"供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。","textEn":"Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting."},{"id":"a006-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「供體可回收性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating plan donor reuse?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"供體再使用需要表面修復與累計厚度帳本。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Donor reuse requires surface recovery and cumulative thickness accounting. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}},{"id":"a006-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-05"],"title":"晶圓配對","titleEn":"Pair donor and handle wafers","objective":"完成「晶圓配對」的工程驗收單，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for pair donor and handle wafers, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶圓配對。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Pair donor and handle wafers. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。 應回到「晶圓配對」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable. Revisit assumptions and sampling for pair donor and handle wafers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶圓配對」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for pair donor and handle wafers: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-06-k1","title":"晶圓配對的原理","titleEn":"Pair donor and handle wafers principle","text":"熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。","textEn":"Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding."},{"id":"a006-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","textEn":"SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶圓配對」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating pair donor and handle wafers?","options":["TTV 與表面粗糙度可以互換。","只量中心厚度即可代表全片形貌。","熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。"],"optionsEn":["TTV and surface roughness are interchangeable.","Center thickness alone represents full-wafer geometry.","Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱膨脹及形貌不相容會影響鍵合品質。 SOI 的支撐晶圓承擔機械功能，埋氧切斷直流通路，頂層提供通道；三者厚度不能只按總厚度驗收。","explanationEn":"Thermal-expansion and shape mismatch can impair bonding. SOI handle, oxide and top silicon provide support, insulation and channels; total thickness alone cannot accept the stack."}}]},{"id":"a006-stage02","order":2,"title":"鍵合與層轉移","titleEn":"Bonding and layer transfer","description":"在「鍵合與層轉移」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for bonding and layer transfer, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a006-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-06"],"title":"離子層深度","titleEn":"Locate the implanted split layer","objective":"完成「離子層深度」的因果圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for locate the implanted split layer, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：離子層深度。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate the implanted split layer. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「離子層深度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate the implanted split layer and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「離子層深度」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for locate the implanted split layer: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-07-k1","title":"離子層深度的原理","titleEn":"Locate the implanted split layer principle","text":"佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。","textEn":"Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty."},{"id":"a006-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「離子層深度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate the implanted split layer?","options":["佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。","晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty.","A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"佈植深度分布決定弱化層位置的不確定度。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Implant depth distribution sets split-layer position uncertainty. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-07"],"title":"活化表面","titleEn":"Compare activated surfaces","objective":"完成「活化表面」的對照表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare activated surfaces, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：活化表面。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare activated surfaces. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「活化表面」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare activated surfaces and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「活化表面」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare activated surfaces: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-08-k1","title":"活化表面的原理","titleEn":"Compare activated surfaces principle","text":"表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。","textEn":"Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness."},{"id":"a006-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「活化表面」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare activated surfaces?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面活化改善接合但也可能改變粗糙度。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Activation can assist bonding while changing surface roughness. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-08"],"title":"顆粒與空洞","titleEn":"Connect particles to voids","objective":"完成「顆粒與空洞」的敏感度草圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for connect particles to voids, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：顆粒與空洞。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Connect particles to voids. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「顆粒與空洞」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for connect particles to voids and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「顆粒與空洞」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for connect particles to voids: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-09-k1","title":"顆粒與空洞的原理","titleEn":"Connect particles to voids principle","text":"單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。","textEn":"One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself."},{"id":"a006-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「顆粒與空洞」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating connect particles to voids?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。","單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness.","One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一顆粒可能造成大於自身尺寸的未鍵合區。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"One particle can create an unbonded region larger than itself. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-09"],"title":"鍵合波前","titleEn":"Track bonding-front propagation","objective":"完成「鍵合波前」的故障判別表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for track bonding-front propagation, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鍵合波前。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track bonding-front propagation. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「鍵合波前」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track bonding-front propagation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鍵合波前」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for track bonding-front propagation: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-10-k1","title":"鍵合波前的原理","titleEn":"Track bonding-front propagation principle","text":"波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。","textEn":"Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems."},{"id":"a006-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鍵合波前」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track bonding-front propagation?","options":["波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。","晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems.","A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"波前不規則可提示局部氣體或接觸問題。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Irregular bonding fronts can indicate trapped gas or contact problems. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-10"],"title":"分裂與熱處理","titleEn":"Separate splitting from strengthening","objective":"完成「分裂與熱處理」的量測規劃，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for separate splitting from strengthening, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：分裂與熱處理。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate splitting from strengthening. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「分裂與熱處理」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate splitting from strengthening and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「分裂與熱處理」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for separate splitting from strengthening: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-11-k1","title":"分裂與熱處理的原理","titleEn":"Separate splitting from strengthening principle","text":"分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。","textEn":"Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface."},{"id":"a006-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「分裂與熱處理」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate splitting from strengthening?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分裂形成薄層，鍵合強化另有介面目標。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Splitting forms the thin layer while bond strengthening targets the interface. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}},{"id":"a006-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-11"],"title":"供體修復","titleEn":"Define donor refresh evidence","objective":"完成「供體修復」的工程驗收單，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for define donor refresh evidence, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：供體修復。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define donor refresh evidence. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。 應回到「供體修復」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define donor refresh evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「供體修復」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for define donor refresh evidence: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-12-k1","title":"供體修復的原理","titleEn":"Define donor refresh evidence principle","text":"再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。","textEn":"Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment."},{"id":"a006-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","textEn":"Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「供體修復」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define donor refresh evidence?","options":["晶圓表面外觀平整就可排除次表面裂紋。","切片厚度就是最終成品厚度。","再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。"],"optionsEn":["A flat-looking surface rules out subsurface cracks.","Sliced thickness equals final finished thickness.","Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"再拋光後需重新確認形貌與殘留損傷。 分裂深度由佈植輪廓及後續演化共同決定；能量設定是輸入，而完成轉移後的厚度圖才是輸出證據。","explanationEn":"Refreshed donors need renewed shape and damage assessment. Splitting depends on implant profiles and later evolution; implant energy is an input while transferred-thickness maps are output evidence."}}]},{"id":"a006-stage03","order":3,"title":"薄層量測","titleEn":"Thin-layer measurements","description":"在「薄層量測」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for thin-layer measurements, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a006-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-12"],"title":"頂矽厚度圖","titleEn":"Map top-silicon thickness","objective":"完成「頂矽厚度圖」的因果圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map top-silicon thickness, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：頂矽厚度圖。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map top-silicon thickness. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「頂矽厚度圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map top-silicon thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「頂矽厚度圖」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map top-silicon thickness: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-13-k1","title":"頂矽厚度圖的原理","titleEn":"Map top-silicon thickness principle","text":"厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。","textEn":"Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation."},{"id":"a006-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「頂矽厚度圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map top-silicon thickness?","options":["厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。","平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation.","Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":0,"explanation":"厚度非均勻可能轉成元件臨界電壓變異。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"Thickness nonuniformity can translate into threshold-voltage variation. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-13"],"title":"埋氧連續性","titleEn":"Inspect buried-oxide continuity","objective":"完成「埋氧連續性」的對照表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for inspect buried-oxide continuity, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：埋氧連續性。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect buried-oxide continuity. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「埋氧連續性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect buried-oxide continuity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「埋氧連續性」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for inspect buried-oxide continuity: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-14-k1","title":"埋氧連續性的原理","titleEn":"Inspect buried-oxide continuity principle","text":"局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。","textEn":"Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths."},{"id":"a006-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「埋氧連續性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect buried-oxide continuity?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部缺陷可能建立不預期的電性路徑。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"Local oxide defects can create unintended electrical paths. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-14"],"title":"鍵合強度分布","titleEn":"Map bond strength","objective":"完成「鍵合強度分布」的敏感度草圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map bond strength, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：鍵合強度分布。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map bond strength. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「鍵合強度分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map bond strength and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「鍵合強度分布」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map bond strength: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-15-k1","title":"鍵合強度分布的原理","titleEn":"Map bond strength principle","text":"局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。","textEn":"One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength."},{"id":"a006-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「鍵合強度分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map bond strength?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。","局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count.","One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部強度不能由單一平均破壞值代表。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"One mean fracture value cannot describe local bond strength. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-15"],"title":"界面陷阱","titleEn":"Assess interface traps","objective":"完成「界面陷阱」的故障判別表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess interface traps, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界面陷阱。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess interface traps. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「界面陷阱」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess interface traps and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界面陷阱」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess interface traps: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-16-k1","title":"界面陷阱的原理","titleEn":"Assess interface traps principle","text":"幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。","textEn":"Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality."},{"id":"a006-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界面陷阱」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess interface traps?","options":["幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。","平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality.","Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何完整不等於界面電性良好。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"Geometric integrity does not establish electrical interface quality. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-16"],"title":"表面粗糙度","titleEn":"Check transferred-surface roughness","objective":"完成「表面粗糙度」的量測規劃，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for check transferred-surface roughness, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面粗糙度。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check transferred-surface roughness. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「表面粗糙度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check transferred-surface roughness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面粗糙度」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for check transferred-surface roughness: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-17-k1","title":"表面粗糙度的原理","titleEn":"Check transferred-surface roughness principle","text":"分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。","textEn":"The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons."},{"id":"a006-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面粗糙度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check transferred-surface roughness?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分裂面與完成拋光面需分別比較。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"The split surface and finished surface require separate comparisons. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}},{"id":"a006-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-17"],"title":"缺陷邊緣排除","titleEn":"Specify edge exclusion","objective":"完成「缺陷邊緣排除」的工程驗收單，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for specify edge exclusion, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：缺陷邊緣排除。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Specify edge exclusion. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。 應回到「缺陷邊緣排除」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions. Revisit assumptions and sampling for specify edge exclusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「缺陷邊緣排除」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for specify edge exclusion: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-18-k1","title":"缺陷邊緣排除的原理","titleEn":"Specify edge exclusion principle","text":"邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。","textEn":"Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area."},{"id":"a006-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","textEn":"Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「缺陷邊緣排除」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating specify edge exclusion?","options":["平均值相同就不必檢查片間分布。","材料移除量不會影響可用晶圓數。","邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。"],"optionsEn":["Equal averages eliminate the need to inspect wafer distributions.","Material removal cannot affect usable wafer count.","Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣未鍵合區需與可用面積一起呈現。 鍵合空洞改變局部機械支撐與熱路徑；即使頂矽厚度正常，局部空洞仍可能影響後續加工。","explanationEn":"Unbonded edges must be reported with usable area. Bond voids alter support and heat paths, so normal top-silicon thickness does not eliminate void-related processing risks."}}]},{"id":"a006-stage04","order":4,"title":"元件相容性","titleEn":"Device compatibility","description":"在「元件相容性」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for device compatibility, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a006-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-18"],"title":"自熱效應","titleEn":"Analyze self-heating","objective":"完成「自熱效應」的因果圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for analyze self-heating, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：自熱效應。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze self-heating. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「自熱效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze self-heating and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「自熱效應」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for analyze self-heating: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-19-k1","title":"自熱效應的原理","titleEn":"Analyze self-heating principle","text":"埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。","textEn":"Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating."},{"id":"a006-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「自熱效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze self-heating?","options":["埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。","局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating.","One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":0,"explanation":"埋氧的熱阻可提高局部溫升。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Buried-oxide thermal resistance can increase local heating. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-19"],"title":"背閘耦合","titleEn":"Trace back-gate coupling","objective":"完成「背閘耦合」的對照表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace back-gate coupling, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：背閘耦合。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace back-gate coupling. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「背閘耦合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace back-gate coupling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「背閘耦合」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace back-gate coupling: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-20-k1","title":"背閘耦合的原理","titleEn":"Trace back-gate coupling principle","text":"支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。","textEn":"Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel."},{"id":"a006-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「背閘耦合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace back-gate coupling?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支撐層電位可透過介電層耦合至通道。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Handle potential can couple through dielectric into the channel. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-20"],"title":"RF 基板差異","titleEn":"Compare RF substrate needs","objective":"完成「RF 基板差異」的敏感度草圖，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare rf substrate needs, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：RF 基板差異。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare RF substrate needs. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「RF 基板差異」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare rf substrate needs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「RF 基板差異」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare rf substrate needs: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-21-k1","title":"RF 基板差異的原理","titleEn":"Compare RF substrate needs principle","text":"高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。","textEn":"High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements."},{"id":"a006-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「RF 基板差異」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare rf substrate needs?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。","高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost.","High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高電阻支撐層與邏輯薄體需求並不等同。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"High-resistivity RF handles and thin-body logic have different requirements. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-21"],"title":"應力翹曲","titleEn":"Assess stress-induced bow","objective":"完成「應力翹曲」的故障判別表，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess stress-induced bow, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應力翹曲。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess stress-induced bow. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「應力翹曲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess stress-induced bow and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應力翹曲」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess stress-induced bow: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-22-k1","title":"應力翹曲的原理","titleEn":"Assess stress-induced bow principle","text":"多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。","textEn":"Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice."},{"id":"a006-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應力翹曲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess stress-induced bow?","options":["多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。","局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice.","One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多層應力平衡取決於厚度與材料組合。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Multilayer stress balance depends on thickness and material choice. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-22"],"title":"分層追溯","titleEn":"Trace layer provenance","objective":"完成「分層追溯」的量測規劃，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for trace layer provenance, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：分層追溯。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace layer provenance. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「分層追溯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace layer provenance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「分層追溯」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for trace layer provenance: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-23-k1","title":"分層追溯的原理","titleEn":"Trace layer provenance principle","text":"頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。","textEn":"Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable."},{"id":"a006-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「分層追溯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace layer provenance?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost."],"answer":1,"explanation":"頂層與支撐層的原始批號都要保留。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Both donor and handle lot identities must remain traceable. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}},{"id":"a006-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-soitec","v8a-sumco","v8a-wafer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a006-v8-23"],"title":"SOI 放行矩陣","titleEn":"Release the SOI stack","objective":"完成「SOI 放行矩陣」的工程驗收單，把頂矽均勻性、埋氧、鍵合空洞中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for release the soi stack, connecting relevant limits in top-silicon uniformity, buried oxide and bond voids to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：SOI 放行矩陣。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Release the SOI stack. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。 應回到「SOI 放行矩陣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement. Revisit assumptions and sampling for release the soi stack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「SOI 放行矩陣」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for release the soi stack: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a006-v8-24-k1","title":"SOI 放行矩陣的原理","titleEn":"Release the SOI stack principle","text":"隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。","textEn":"Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review."},{"id":"a006-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","textEn":"Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「SOI 放行矩陣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating release the soi stack?","options":["局部截面合格就能取代整片量測。","所有表面缺陷都能由後段拋光無代價消除。","隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。"],"optionsEn":["One acceptable section replaces full-wafer measurement.","All surface defects can be removed by later polishing without cost.","Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔離、薄層均勻、鍵合與熱管理需共同審查。 埋氧抑制電性耦合的同時也增加垂直熱阻，薄體電晶體的電性比較應包含自熱條件。","explanationEn":"Isolation, layer uniformity, bonding and thermal behavior require joint review. Buried oxide reduces electrical coupling while adding vertical thermal resistance; thin-body comparisons should include self-heating."}}]}],"subcategory":"substrate","subcategoryTitle":"晶圓與基板","subcategoryTitleEn":"Wafers and substrates"},{"id":"a007","title":"晶圓表面清洗","titleEn":"Wafer surface cleaning","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解去污效果、材料損失、再污染，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore removal, material loss and recontamination through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["污染與表面目標","清洗路徑","沖洗乾燥","潔淨證據"],"labelsEn":["Contaminants and surface targets","Cleaning pathways","Rinsing and drying","Cleanliness evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a007-stage01","order":1,"title":"污染與表面目標","titleEn":"Contaminants and surface targets","description":"在「污染與表面目標」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for contaminants and surface targets, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a007-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"污染分類","titleEn":"Classify contaminants","objective":"完成「污染分類」的因果圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for classify contaminants, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：污染分類。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Classify contaminants. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「污染分類」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for classify contaminants and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「污染分類」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for classify contaminants: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-01-k1","title":"污染分類的原理","titleEn":"Classify contaminants principle","text":"粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。","textEn":"Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence."},{"id":"a007-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「污染分類」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating classify contaminants?","options":["粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"粒子、金屬、有機物與原生氧化層需要不同證據。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Particles, metals, organics and native oxide need different evidence. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-01"],"title":"基底相容表","titleEn":"Build substrate compatibility tables","objective":"完成「基底相容表」的對照表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for build substrate compatibility tables, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：基底相容表。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build substrate compatibility tables. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「基底相容表」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build substrate compatibility tables and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「基底相容表」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for build substrate compatibility tables: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-02-k1","title":"基底相容表的原理","titleEn":"Build substrate compatibility tables principle","text":"能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。","textEn":"A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films."},{"id":"a007-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「基底相容表」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build substrate compatibility tables?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"能去除污染的處理也可能侵蝕功能薄膜。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"A contaminant-removing treatment may also attack functional films. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-02"],"title":"先後順序圖","titleEn":"Map cleaning order","objective":"完成「先後順序圖」的敏感度草圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map cleaning order, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：先後順序圖。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map cleaning order. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Each surface state affects the next cleaning step. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Each surface state affects the next cleaning step. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「先後順序圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map cleaning order and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「先後順序圖」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map cleaning order: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-03-k1","title":"先後順序圖的原理","titleEn":"Map cleaning order principle","text":"前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。","textEn":"Each surface state affects the next cleaning step."},{"id":"a007-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「先後順序圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map cleaning order?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Each surface state affects the next cleaning step."],"answer":2,"explanation":"前一步產生的表面狀態會影響後一步。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Each surface state affects the next cleaning step. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-03"],"title":"空白見證片","titleEn":"Choose blank witnesses","objective":"完成「空白見證片」的故障判別表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for choose blank witnesses, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：空白見證片。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose blank witnesses. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Containers and handling contribute background contamination. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Containers and handling contribute background contamination. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「空白見證片」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose blank witnesses and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「空白見證片」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for choose blank witnesses: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-04-k1","title":"空白見證片的原理","titleEn":"Choose blank witnesses principle","text":"容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。","textEn":"Containers and handling contribute background contamination."},{"id":"a007-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「空白見證片」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose blank witnesses?","options":["容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Containers and handling contribute background contamination.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"容器與搬運也會貢獻背景污染。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Containers and handling contribute background contamination. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-04"],"title":"潔淨程度指標","titleEn":"Select cleanliness metrics","objective":"完成「潔淨程度指標」的量測規劃，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for select cleanliness metrics, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：潔淨程度指標。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Select cleanliness metrics. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「潔淨程度指標」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for select cleanliness metrics and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「潔淨程度指標」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for select cleanliness metrics: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-05-k1","title":"潔淨程度指標的原理","titleEn":"Select cleanliness metrics principle","text":"粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。","textEn":"Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration."},{"id":"a007-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「潔淨程度指標」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating select cleanliness metrics?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粒子數不能代表金屬濃度。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Particle counts cannot represent metal concentration. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}},{"id":"a007-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-05"],"title":"接觸角限制","titleEn":"Bound contact-angle interpretation","objective":"完成「接觸角限制」的工程驗收單，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for bound contact-angle interpretation, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸角限制。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Bound contact-angle interpretation. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「接觸角限制」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for bound contact-angle interpretation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸角限制」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for bound contact-angle interpretation: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-06-k1","title":"接觸角限制的原理","titleEn":"Bound contact-angle interpretation principle","text":"接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。","textEn":"Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence."},{"id":"a007-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","textEn":"Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸角限制」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating bound contact-angle interpretation?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸角反映濕潤狀態，不能單獨證明無污染。 去除目標可能是表面粒子、溶解金屬或反應殘留；同一粒子掃描器不能提供這三者完整證據。","explanationEn":"Contact angle reflects wetting but cannot prove contaminant absence. Targets may be particles, dissolved metals or reaction residues; one particle scanner cannot fully characterize all three."}}]},{"id":"a007-stage02","order":2,"title":"清洗路徑","titleEn":"Cleaning pathways","description":"在「清洗路徑」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for cleaning pathways, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a007-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-06"],"title":"化學選擇性","titleEn":"Assess chemical selectivity","objective":"完成「化學選擇性」的因果圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess chemical selectivity, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：化學選擇性。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess chemical selectivity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「化學選擇性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess chemical selectivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「化學選擇性」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess chemical selectivity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-07-k1","title":"化學選擇性的原理","titleEn":"Assess chemical selectivity principle","text":"選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。","textEn":"Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss."},{"id":"a007-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「化學選擇性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess chemical selectivity?","options":["選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"選擇性需同時計入污染移除及基底損失。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Selectivity includes contaminant removal and substrate loss. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-07"],"title":"粒子附著力","titleEn":"Draw particle adhesion forces","objective":"完成「粒子附著力」的對照表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for draw particle adhesion forces, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：粒子附著力。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw particle adhesion forces. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「粒子附著力」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw particle adhesion forces and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「粒子附著力」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for draw particle adhesion forces: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-08-k1","title":"粒子附著力的原理","titleEn":"Draw particle adhesion forces principle","text":"粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。","textEn":"Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty."},{"id":"a007-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「粒子附著力」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw particle adhesion forces?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粒子尺寸與表面化學會改變去除難度。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Particle size and surface chemistry alter removal difficulty. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-08"],"title":"邊界層更新","titleEn":"Analyze boundary-layer renewal","objective":"完成「邊界層更新」的敏感度草圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for analyze boundary-layer renewal, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊界層更新。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze boundary-layer renewal. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Flow affects reactant supply and product removal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Flow affects reactant supply and product removal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「邊界層更新」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze boundary-layer renewal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊界層更新」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for analyze boundary-layer renewal: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-09-k1","title":"邊界層更新的原理","titleEn":"Analyze boundary-layer renewal principle","text":"流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。","textEn":"Flow affects reactant supply and product removal."},{"id":"a007-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊界層更新」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze boundary-layer renewal?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Flow affects reactant supply and product removal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"流場影響反應物供給與產物移除。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Flow affects reactant supply and product removal. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-09"],"title":"超音波副作用","titleEn":"Assess acoustic side effects","objective":"完成「超音波副作用」的故障判別表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess acoustic side effects, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：超音波副作用。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess acoustic side effects. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「超音波副作用」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess acoustic side effects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「超音波副作用」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess acoustic side effects: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-10-k1","title":"超音波副作用的原理","titleEn":"Assess acoustic side effects principle","text":"提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。","textEn":"Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures."},{"id":"a007-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「超音波副作用」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess acoustic side effects?","options":["提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"提升去粒能力也可能傷害細長結構。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Stronger acoustic removal may damage slender structures. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-10"],"title":"槽液老化","titleEn":"Track bath aging","objective":"完成「槽液老化」的量測規劃，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for track bath aging, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：槽液老化。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track bath aging. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「槽液老化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track bath aging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「槽液老化」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for track bath aging: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-11-k1","title":"槽液老化的原理","titleEn":"Track bath aging principle","text":"溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。","textEn":"Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry."},{"id":"a007-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「槽液老化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track bath aging?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溶解污染累積使新液與使用後槽液不同。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Accumulated contaminants make used baths differ from fresh chemistry. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}},{"id":"a007-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-11"],"title":"單片與批次","titleEn":"Compare single-wafer and batch cleaning","objective":"完成「單片與批次」的工程驗收單，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compare single-wafer and batch cleaning, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：單片與批次。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare single-wafer and batch cleaning. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「單片與批次」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare single-wafer and batch cleaning and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「單片與批次」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compare single-wafer and batch cleaning: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-12-k1","title":"單片與批次的原理","titleEn":"Compare single-wafer and batch cleaning principle","text":"批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。","textEn":"Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis."},{"id":"a007-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","textEn":"Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「單片與批次」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare single-wafer and batch cleaning?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"批次共用液體需要考慮片間交叉污染。 表面反應後的產物仍須移出邊界層；化學反應完成不代表表面已沒有可再沉積物。","explanationEn":"Shared batch liquids require inter-wafer contamination analysis. Reaction products must leave the boundary layer; completed chemistry does not imply no redepositable material remains."}}]},{"id":"a007-stage03","order":3,"title":"沖洗乾燥","titleEn":"Rinsing and drying","description":"在「沖洗乾燥」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for rinsing and drying, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a007-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-12"],"title":"沖洗置換模型","titleEn":"Model rinse displacement","objective":"完成「沖洗置換模型」的因果圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for model rinse displacement, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：沖洗置換模型。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Model rinse displacement. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「沖洗置換模型」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for model rinse displacement and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「沖洗置換模型」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for model rinse displacement: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-13-k1","title":"沖洗置換模型的原理","titleEn":"Model rinse displacement principle","text":"僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。","textEn":"Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions."},{"id":"a007-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「沖洗置換模型」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating model rinse displacement?","options":["僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"僅靠出口平均值可能漏掉滯留區。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Outlet averages can miss stagnant regions. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-13"],"title":"水質進入點","titleEn":"Check incoming rinse quality","objective":"完成「水質進入點」的對照表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for check incoming rinse quality, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：水質進入點。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check incoming rinse quality. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「水質進入點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check incoming rinse quality and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「水質進入點」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for check incoming rinse quality: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-14-k1","title":"水質進入點的原理","titleEn":"Check incoming rinse quality principle","text":"清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。","textEn":"Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality."},{"id":"a007-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「水質進入點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check incoming rinse quality?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清洗末段也可能由水質帶回污染。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Final rinsing can reintroduce contamination through water quality. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-14"],"title":"殘液乾燥痕","titleEn":"Interpret drying marks","objective":"完成「殘液乾燥痕」的敏感度草圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for interpret drying marks, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：殘液乾燥痕。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret drying marks. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「殘液乾燥痕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret drying marks and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「殘液乾燥痕」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for interpret drying marks: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-15-k1","title":"殘液乾燥痕的原理","titleEn":"Interpret drying marks principle","text":"水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。","textEn":"Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects."},{"id":"a007-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「殘液乾燥痕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret drying marks?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水痕可來自殘液濃縮而非原本薄膜缺陷。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Drying marks can result from concentrated residue rather than film defects. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-15"],"title":"毛細倒塌","titleEn":"Assess capillary collapse","objective":"完成「毛細倒塌」的故障判別表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess capillary collapse, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：毛細倒塌。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess capillary collapse. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「毛細倒塌」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess capillary collapse and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「毛細倒塌」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess capillary collapse: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-16-k1","title":"毛細倒塌的原理","titleEn":"Assess capillary collapse principle","text":"液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。","textEn":"Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features."},{"id":"a007-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「毛細倒塌」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess capillary collapse?","options":["液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"液面收縮力對高深寬比結構尤其重要。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Receding-meniscus forces matter strongly for high-aspect-ratio features. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-16"],"title":"等待時間控制","titleEn":"Control queue-time evidence","objective":"完成「等待時間控制」的量測規劃，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for control queue-time evidence, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：等待時間控制。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Control queue-time evidence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Post-dry exposure changes readsorption. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Post-dry exposure changes readsorption. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「等待時間控制」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for control queue-time evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「等待時間控制」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for control queue-time evidence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-17-k1","title":"等待時間控制的原理","titleEn":"Control queue-time evidence principle","text":"乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。","textEn":"Post-dry exposure changes readsorption."},{"id":"a007-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「等待時間控制」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating control queue-time evidence?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Post-dry exposure changes readsorption.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"乾燥後的暴露時間會改變再吸附。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Post-dry exposure changes readsorption. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}},{"id":"a007-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-17"],"title":"搬運接觸點","titleEn":"Trace handling contact points","objective":"完成「搬運接觸點」的工程驗收單，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for trace handling contact points, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運接觸點。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace handling contact points. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「搬運接觸點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace handling contact points and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運接觸點」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for trace handling contact points: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-18-k1","title":"搬運接觸點的原理","titleEn":"Trace handling contact points principle","text":"背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。","textEn":"Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment."},{"id":"a007-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","textEn":"Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運接觸點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace handling contact points?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"背面接觸污染仍可透過設備傳播。 乾燥時液體體積下降會濃縮不揮發物，毛細力又可能使細長結構變形，兩種失效需分開觀察。","explanationEn":"Backside contact contamination can spread through equipment. Drying concentrates nonvolatile residues and generates capillary deformation; these failure mechanisms need separate observations."}}]},{"id":"a007-stage04","order":4,"title":"潔淨證據","titleEn":"Cleanliness evidence","description":"在「潔淨證據」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for cleanliness evidence, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a007-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-18"],"title":"前後粒子差","titleEn":"Calculate particle adders","objective":"完成「前後粒子差」的因果圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for calculate particle adders, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：前後粒子差。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂缺陷圖：同一掃描區清洗前 40 顆、後 18 顆，其中 10 顆位置重合。分開計算留存、移除與新生顆粒；說明為何只相減會漏掉新增污染。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Calculate particle adders. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical matched defect maps: 40 particles before, 18 after, with 10 co-located. Separate retained, removed and added particles and explain why simple subtraction hides new contamination.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「前後粒子差」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for calculate particle adders and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「前後粒子差」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for calculate particle adders: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-19-k1","title":"前後粒子差的原理","titleEn":"Calculate particle adders principle","text":"比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。","textEn":"Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds."},{"id":"a007-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「前後粒子差」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating calculate particle adders?","options":["比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較必須匹配同一掃描範圍與門檻。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Before-after counts need matching scan areas and thresholds. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-19"],"title":"金屬分析空白","titleEn":"Audit metal-analysis blanks","objective":"完成「金屬分析空白」的對照表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for audit metal-analysis blanks, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬分析空白。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Audit metal-analysis blanks. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「金屬分析空白」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for audit metal-analysis blanks and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬分析空白」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for audit metal-analysis blanks: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-20-k1","title":"金屬分析空白的原理","titleEn":"Audit metal-analysis blanks principle","text":"低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。","textEn":"Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits."},{"id":"a007-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬分析空白」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating audit metal-analysis blanks?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低濃度量測需要容器空白與方法檢出限。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Trace analysis needs container blanks and detection limits. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-20"],"title":"表面損失圖","titleEn":"Map substrate loss","objective":"完成「表面損失圖」的敏感度草圖，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map substrate loss, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面損失圖。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map substrate loss. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「表面損失圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map substrate loss and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面損失圖」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map substrate loss: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-21-k1","title":"表面損失圖的原理","titleEn":"Map substrate loss principle","text":"去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。","textEn":"Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss."},{"id":"a007-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面損失圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map substrate loss?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"去污有效仍需證明功能材料損失可接受。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Effective cleaning still requires acceptable functional-material loss. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-21"],"title":"缺陷空間關聯","titleEn":"Correlate defect locations","objective":"完成「缺陷空間關聯」的故障判別表，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for correlate defect locations, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：缺陷空間關聯。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Correlate defect locations. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「缺陷空間關聯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for correlate defect locations and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「缺陷空間關聯」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for correlate defect locations: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-22-k1","title":"缺陷空間關聯的原理","titleEn":"Correlate defect locations principle","text":"位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。","textEn":"Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone."},{"id":"a007-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「缺陷空間關聯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating correlate defect locations?","options":["位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"位置關聯能引導排查，不能獨自證明因果。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Spatial correlation guides diagnosis but does not establish causality alone. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-22"],"title":"重工邊界","titleEn":"Define rework limits","objective":"完成「重工邊界」的量測規劃，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define rework limits, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：重工邊界。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define rework limits. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「重工邊界」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define rework limits and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「重工邊界」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define rework limits: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-23-k1","title":"重工邊界的原理","titleEn":"Define rework limits principle","text":"反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。","textEn":"Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss."},{"id":"a007-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「重工邊界」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define rework limits?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"反覆清洗的累積損失可能不可逆。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Repeated cleaning can cause irreversible cumulative loss. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}},{"id":"a007-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-clean","v8a-purity","v8a-mit"],"prerequisiteIds":["a007-v8-23"],"title":"潔淨交接單","titleEn":"Complete the cleanliness handoff","objective":"完成「潔淨交接單」的工程驗收單，把去污效果、材料損失、再污染中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for complete the cleanliness handoff, connecting relevant limits in removal, material loss and recontamination to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：潔淨交接單。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Complete the cleanliness handoff. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「潔淨交接單」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for complete the cleanliness handoff and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「潔淨交接單」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for complete the cleanliness handoff: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a007-v8-24-k1","title":"潔淨交接單的原理","titleEn":"Complete the cleanliness handoff principle","text":"移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。","textEn":"Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff."},{"id":"a007-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","textEn":"Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「潔淨交接單」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating complete the cleanliness handoff?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移除效果、表面變化及等待上限應一併交付。 清潔驗收要比較污染減少與基底消耗，並確認搬運及排隊後的表面仍符合下一模組要求。","explanationEn":"Removal, surface change and queue limits belong in the handoff. Cleaning acceptance balances contaminant removal against substrate consumption and verifies the surface after transport and queueing."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"a008","title":"超純水供應系統","titleEn":"Ultrapure-water supply systems","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解水質多指標、使用點、滯留，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["用水需求與污染","純化系統分工","循環與監測","異常及永續"],"labelsEn":["Water demand and contaminants","Purification functions","Distribution and monitoring","Excursions and sustainability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a008-stage01","order":1,"title":"用水需求與污染","titleEn":"Water demand and contaminants","description":"在「用水需求與污染」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for water demand and contaminants, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a008-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"界定使用點","titleEn":"Define points of use","objective":"完成「界定使用點」的因果圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define points of use, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界定使用點。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define points of use. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「界定使用點」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define points of use and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界定使用點」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define points of use: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-01-k1","title":"界定使用點的原理","titleEn":"Define points of use principle","text":"沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。","textEn":"Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality."},{"id":"a008-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界定使用點」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define points of use?","options":["沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沖洗、配液與設備用水可能有不同品質要求。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"Rinsing, blending and utilities can require different water quality. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-01"],"title":"峰值與平均流量","titleEn":"Separate peak and average flow","objective":"完成「峰值與平均流量」的對照表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate peak and average flow, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：峰值與平均流量。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate peak and average flow. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Average demand misses coincident usage peaks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Average demand misses coincident usage peaks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「峰值與平均流量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate peak and average flow and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「峰值與平均流量」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate peak and average flow: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-02-k1","title":"峰值與平均流量的原理","titleEn":"Separate peak and average flow principle","text":"只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。","textEn":"Average demand misses coincident usage peaks."},{"id":"a008-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「峰值與平均流量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate peak and average flow?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Average demand misses coincident usage peaks.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只按平均需求設計會漏掉同步用水尖峰。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"Average demand misses coincident usage peaks. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-02"],"title":"污染質量帳","titleEn":"Build contaminant mass balances","objective":"完成「污染質量帳」的敏感度草圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for build contaminant mass balances, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：污染質量帳。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build contaminant mass balances. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「污染質量帳」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build contaminant mass balances and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「污染質量帳」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for build contaminant mass balances: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-03-k1","title":"污染質量帳的原理","titleEn":"Build contaminant mass balances principle","text":"濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。","textEn":"Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux."},{"id":"a008-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「污染質量帳」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build contaminant mass balances?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux."],"answer":2,"explanation":"濃度必須與流量合用才能換算污染通量。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"Concentration and flow jointly determine contaminant flux. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-03"],"title":"電阻率盲區","titleEn":"Identify resistivity blind spots","objective":"完成「電阻率盲區」的故障判別表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for identify resistivity blind spots, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電阻率盲區。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify resistivity blind spots. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「電阻率盲區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify resistivity blind spots and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電阻率盲區」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for identify resistivity blind spots: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-04-k1","title":"電阻率盲區的原理","titleEn":"Identify resistivity blind spots principle","text":"高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。","textEn":"High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles."},{"id":"a008-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電阻率盲區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify resistivity blind spots?","options":["高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高電阻率不能排除非離子有機物或粒子。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"High resistivity does not exclude neutral organics or particles. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-04"],"title":"TOC 指標","titleEn":"Interpret total organic carbon","objective":"完成「TOC 指標」的量測規劃，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for interpret total organic carbon, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：TOC 指標。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret total organic carbon. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「TOC 指標」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret total organic carbon and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「TOC 指標」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for interpret total organic carbon: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-05-k1","title":"TOC 指標的原理","titleEn":"Interpret total organic carbon principle","text":"TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。","textEn":"TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity."},{"id":"a008-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「TOC 指標」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret total organic carbon?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"TOC 是總量指標而不是個別化合物身分。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"TOC measures aggregate carbon, not compound identity. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}},{"id":"a008-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-05"],"title":"回用水分流","titleEn":"Segregate recovery streams","objective":"完成「回用水分流」的工程驗收單，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for segregate recovery streams, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：回用水分流。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Segregate recovery streams. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「回用水分流」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for segregate recovery streams and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「回用水分流」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for segregate recovery streams: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-06-k1","title":"回用水分流的原理","titleEn":"Segregate recovery streams principle","text":"回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。","textEn":"Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load."},{"id":"a008-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","textEn":"Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「回用水分流」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating segregate recovery streams?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load."],"answer":2,"explanation":"回收前需區分不同製程流的污染負荷。 污染物質量流率為濃度乘流量；濃度相同時，大流量使用點可能接收更大的污染總量。","explanationEn":"Recovery requires segregation by process contaminant load. Contaminant mass flow is concentration times flow, so a high-flow outlet can receive more contaminant at equal concentration."}}]},{"id":"a008-stage02","order":2,"title":"純化系統分工","titleEn":"Purification functions","description":"在「純化系統分工」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for purification functions, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a008-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-06"],"title":"前處理功能","titleEn":"Assign pretreatment functions","objective":"完成「前處理功能」的因果圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assign pretreatment functions, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：前處理功能。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign pretreatment functions. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「前處理功能」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign pretreatment functions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「前處理功能」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assign pretreatment functions: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-07-k1","title":"前處理功能的原理","titleEn":"Assign pretreatment functions principle","text":"前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。","textEn":"Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing."},{"id":"a008-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「前處理功能」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign pretreatment functions?","options":["前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"前處理保護後段膜與樹脂，不等於末端純化。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Pretreatment protects downstream media but is not final polishing. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-07"],"title":"逆滲透物料平衡","titleEn":"Balance reverse-osmosis streams","objective":"完成「逆滲透物料平衡」的對照表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for balance reverse-osmosis streams, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：逆滲透物料平衡。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂守恆題：進水 100 L/min、產水 75 L/min、濃水 25 L/min；在無其他支流假設下檢查流量守恆及回收率，另列污染濃度資料才能求質量流率。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Balance reverse-osmosis streams. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical balance: feed 100 L/min, permeate 75 L/min and concentrate 25 L/min. Check flow conservation and recovery assuming no other streams; list concentration data needed for contaminant mass balance.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「逆滲透物料平衡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for balance reverse-osmosis streams and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「逆滲透物料平衡」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for balance reverse-osmosis streams: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-08-k1","title":"逆滲透物料平衡的原理","titleEn":"Balance reverse-osmosis streams principle","text":"產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。","textEn":"Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance."},{"id":"a008-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「逆滲透物料平衡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating balance reverse-osmosis streams?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"產水、濃水與進水必須符合質量守恆。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Permeate, concentrate and feed must satisfy mass balance. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-08"],"title":"離子交換突破","titleEn":"Interpret ion-exchange breakthrough","objective":"完成「離子交換突破」的敏感度草圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for interpret ion-exchange breakthrough, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：離子交換突破。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret ion-exchange breakthrough. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「離子交換突破」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret ion-exchange breakthrough and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「離子交換突破」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for interpret ion-exchange breakthrough: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-09-k1","title":"離子交換突破的原理","titleEn":"Interpret ion-exchange breakthrough principle","text":"樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。","textEn":"Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion."},{"id":"a008-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「離子交換突破」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret ion-exchange breakthrough?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"樹脂接近耗盡時出水變化可能早於總體失效。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Effluent changes can precede full resin exhaustion. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-09"],"title":"有機物分解","titleEn":"Assess organic-removal stages","objective":"完成「有機物分解」的故障判別表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess organic-removal stages, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：有機物分解。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess organic-removal stages. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「有機物分解」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess organic-removal stages and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「有機物分解」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess organic-removal stages: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-10-k1","title":"有機物分解的原理","titleEn":"Assess organic-removal stages principle","text":"分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。","textEn":"Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal."},{"id":"a008-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「有機物分解」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess organic-removal stages?","options":["分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分解有機物可能生成需再去除的離子。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Organic decomposition can produce ions needing subsequent removal. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-10"],"title":"脫氣模組","titleEn":"Evaluate degassing","objective":"完成「脫氣模組」的量測規劃，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for evaluate degassing, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：脫氣模組。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Evaluate degassing. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「脫氣模組」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for evaluate degassing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「脫氣模組」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for evaluate degassing: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-11-k1","title":"脫氣模組的原理","titleEn":"Evaluate degassing principle","text":"溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。","textEn":"Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms."},{"id":"a008-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「脫氣模組」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating evaluate degassing?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溶解氣體與液中粒子使用不同去除機制。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Dissolved gases and particles require different removal mechanisms. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}},{"id":"a008-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-11"],"title":"終端過濾","titleEn":"Review final filtration","objective":"完成「終端過濾」的工程驗收單，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review final filtration, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：終端過濾。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review final filtration. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「終端過濾」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review final filtration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「終端過濾」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review final filtration: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-12-k1","title":"終端過濾的原理","titleEn":"Review final filtration principle","text":"標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。","textEn":"Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency."},{"id":"a008-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","textEn":"Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「終端過濾」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review final filtration?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency."],"answer":2,"explanation":"標稱截留尺寸不是所有污染物的保證去除率。 反滲透、離子交換與終端過濾針對不同物種；串聯設計需要追蹤每段去除及新引入的污染。","explanationEn":"Nominal retention size is not universal contaminant removal efficiency. Reverse osmosis, ion exchange and final filtration target different species; track both removal and added contamination at every stage."}}]},{"id":"a008-stage03","order":3,"title":"循環與監測","titleEn":"Distribution and monitoring","description":"在「循環與監測」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for distribution and monitoring, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a008-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-12"],"title":"循環管網","titleEn":"Trace the recirculation loop","objective":"完成「循環管網」的因果圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace the recirculation loop, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：循環管網。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace the recirculation loop. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「循環管網」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace the recirculation loop and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「循環管網」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace the recirculation loop: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-13-k1","title":"循環管網的原理","titleEn":"Trace the recirculation loop principle","text":"持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。","textEn":"Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness."},{"id":"a008-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「循環管網」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace the recirculation loop?","options":["持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"持續循環降低滯留但不能代替材料潔淨度。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Recirculation reduces stagnation but cannot replace material cleanliness. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-13"],"title":"死角支管","titleEn":"Find dead legs","objective":"完成「死角支管」的對照表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for find dead legs, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：死角支管。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Find dead legs. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Stagnant branches can become contamination sources. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Stagnant branches can become contamination sources. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「死角支管」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for find dead legs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「死角支管」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for find dead legs: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-14-k1","title":"死角支管的原理","titleEn":"Find dead legs principle","text":"低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。","textEn":"Stagnant branches can become contamination sources."},{"id":"a008-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「死角支管」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating find dead legs?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stagnant branches can become contamination sources.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低流速滯留區可成為品質波動來源。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Stagnant branches can become contamination sources. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-14"],"title":"壓差與濾芯","titleEn":"Interpret filter pressure drop","objective":"完成「壓差與濾芯」的敏感度草圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for interpret filter pressure drop, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：壓差與濾芯。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret filter pressure drop. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「壓差與濾芯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret filter pressure drop and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「壓差與濾芯」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for interpret filter pressure drop: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-15-k1","title":"壓差與濾芯的原理","titleEn":"Interpret filter pressure drop principle","text":"壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。","textEn":"Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass."},{"id":"a008-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「壓差與濾芯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret filter pressure drop?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壓差上升可提示負載，低壓差不證明無旁通。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Rising pressure drop suggests loading; low drop does not exclude bypass. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-15"],"title":"使用點採樣","titleEn":"Design point-of-use sampling","objective":"完成「使用點採樣」的故障判別表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for design point-of-use sampling, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：使用點採樣。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Design point-of-use sampling. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「使用點採樣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for design point-of-use sampling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「使用點採樣」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for design point-of-use sampling: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-16-k1","title":"使用點採樣的原理","titleEn":"Design point-of-use sampling principle","text":"中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。","textEn":"Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements."},{"id":"a008-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「使用點採樣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating design point-of-use sampling?","options":["中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"中央水站合格不代表所有末端合格。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Central quality does not prove every outlet meets requirements. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-16"],"title":"感測器延遲","titleEn":"Account for sensor delay","objective":"完成「感測器延遲」的量測規劃，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for account for sensor delay, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：感測器延遲。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Account for sensor delay. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「感測器延遲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for account for sensor delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「感測器延遲」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for account for sensor delay: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-17-k1","title":"感測器延遲的原理","titleEn":"Account for sensor delay principle","text":"採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。","textEn":"Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm."},{"id":"a008-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「感測器延遲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating account for sensor delay?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"採樣管滯留時間會延後警報所代表的事件。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Sample-line residence time delays the event represented by an alarm. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}},{"id":"a008-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-17"],"title":"溫度補償","titleEn":"Review temperature compensation","objective":"完成「溫度補償」的工程驗收單，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review temperature compensation, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度補償。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review temperature compensation. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「溫度補償」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review temperature compensation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度補償」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review temperature compensation: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-18-k1","title":"溫度補償的原理","titleEn":"Review temperature compensation principle","text":"電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。","textEn":"Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata."},{"id":"a008-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","textEn":"Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度補償」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review temperature compensation?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電性讀值須與溫度及補償方法一起記錄。 循環管內停留時間會把源頭事件延遲至使用點，警報回溯須把管內容積與流量納入。","explanationEn":"Electrical readings need temperature and compensation metadata. Pipe residence time delays source events at outlets; excursion tracing needs pipe volume and flow."}}]},{"id":"a008-stage04","order":4,"title":"異常及永續","titleEn":"Excursions and sustainability","description":"在「異常及永續」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for excursions and sustainability, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a008-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-18"],"title":"異常隔離區","titleEn":"Define excursion boundaries","objective":"完成「異常隔離區」的因果圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define excursion boundaries, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：異常隔離區。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define excursion boundaries. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「異常隔離區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define excursion boundaries and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「異常隔離區」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define excursion boundaries: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-19-k1","title":"異常隔離區的原理","titleEn":"Define excursion boundaries principle","text":"受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。","textEn":"Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window."},{"id":"a008-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「異常隔離區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define excursion boundaries?","options":["受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"受影響晶圓需依暴露時間窗回溯。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"Affected wafers should be traced through the exposure time window. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-19"],"title":"維護沖洗證據","titleEn":"Verify maintenance flushing","objective":"完成「維護沖洗證據」的對照表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for verify maintenance flushing, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：維護沖洗證據。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Verify maintenance flushing. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「維護沖洗證據」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for verify maintenance flushing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「維護沖洗證據」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for verify maintenance flushing: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-20-k1","title":"維護沖洗證據的原理","titleEn":"Verify maintenance flushing principle","text":"更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。","textEn":"After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline."},{"id":"a008-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「維護沖洗證據」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating verify maintenance flushing?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"更換零件後需確認釋出污染與背景恢復。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"After replacement, check leachables and return to baseline. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-20"],"title":"多指標交叉驗證","titleEn":"Cross-check quality indicators","objective":"完成「多指標交叉驗證」的敏感度草圖，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for cross-check quality indicators, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：多指標交叉驗證。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Cross-check quality indicators. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「多指標交叉驗證」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for cross-check quality indicators and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「多指標交叉驗證」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for cross-check quality indicators: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-21-k1","title":"多指標交叉驗證的原理","titleEn":"Cross-check quality indicators principle","text":"單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。","textEn":"A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor."},{"id":"a008-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「多指標交叉驗證」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating cross-check quality indicators?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一感測器失效不能由其自身趨勢排除。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"A sensor trend cannot rule out failure of that same sensor. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-21"],"title":"回收率權衡","titleEn":"Assess recovery tradeoffs","objective":"完成「回收率權衡」的故障判別表，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess recovery tradeoffs, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：回收率權衡。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess recovery tradeoffs. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「回收率權衡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess recovery tradeoffs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「回收率權衡」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess recovery tradeoffs: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-22-k1","title":"回收率權衡的原理","titleEn":"Assess recovery tradeoffs principle","text":"提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。","textEn":"Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden."},{"id":"a008-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「回收率權衡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess recovery tradeoffs?","options":["提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"提高回收率可能增加濃縮負荷及能耗。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"Higher recovery can increase concentration and energy burden. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-22"],"title":"停機重啟","titleEn":"Plan restart qualification","objective":"完成「停機重啟」的量測規劃，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for plan restart qualification, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：停機重啟。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Plan restart qualification. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「停機重啟」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for plan restart qualification and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「停機重啟」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for plan restart qualification: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-23-k1","title":"停機重啟的原理","titleEn":"Plan restart qualification principle","text":"停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。","textEn":"Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence."},{"id":"a008-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「停機重啟」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating plan restart qualification?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"停滯後重啟需要重新建立末端品質證據。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"Restart after stagnation needs renewed outlet-quality evidence. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}},{"id":"a008-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-purity","v8a-filtration","v8a-clean","v8a-upw","v8a-upworgano"],"prerequisiteIds":["a008-v8-23"],"title":"水務放行報告","titleEn":"Assemble water-system acceptance","objective":"完成「水務放行報告」的工程驗收單，把水質多指標、使用點、滯留中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assemble water-system acceptance, connecting relevant limits in water-quality indicators, points of use and stagnation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：水務放行報告。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assemble water-system acceptance. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「水務放行報告」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assemble water-system acceptance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「水務放行報告」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assemble water-system acceptance: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a008-v8-24-k1","title":"水務放行報告的原理","titleEn":"Assemble water-system acceptance principle","text":"品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。","textEn":"Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability."},{"id":"a008-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","textEn":"Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「水務放行報告」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assemble water-system acceptance?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"品質、供應穩定、採樣及異常追溯須同時成立。 回收率提高通常降低排放體積，卻可能增加濃水負荷與純化難度，因此水量與品質需共同平衡。","explanationEn":"Acceptance needs quality, supply stability, sampling and excursion traceability. Higher recovery reduces discharge volume but can increase concentrate burden and purification difficulty, requiring joint quantity-quality balancing."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"a009","title":"晶圓廠微污染控制","titleEn":"Microcontamination control in fabs","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore sources, transport and defect maps through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["污染源與路徑","空氣與微環境","液體接觸鏈","缺陷歸因"],"labelsEn":["Sources and pathways","Air and microenvironments","Liquid-contact chains","Defect attribution"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a009-stage01","order":1,"title":"污染源與路徑","titleEn":"Sources and pathways","description":"在「污染源與路徑」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for sources and pathways, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a009-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"建立污染源地圖","titleEn":"Map contamination sources","objective":"完成「建立污染源地圖」的因果圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map contamination sources, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：建立污染源地圖。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map contamination sources. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「建立污染源地圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map contamination sources and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「建立污染源地圖」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map contamination sources: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-01-k1","title":"建立污染源地圖的原理","titleEn":"Map contamination sources principle","text":"人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。","textEn":"People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources."},{"id":"a009-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「建立污染源地圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map contamination sources?","options":["人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"人員、設備、氣體、液體與載具都是可能來源。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"People, tools, gases, liquids and carriers are possible sources. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-01"],"title":"尺寸與危害","titleEn":"Separate size and hazard","objective":"完成「尺寸與危害」的對照表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate size and hazard, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：尺寸與危害。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate size and hazard. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「尺寸與危害」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate size and hazard and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「尺寸與危害」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate size and hazard: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-02-k1","title":"尺寸與危害的原理","titleEn":"Separate size and hazard principle","text":"相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。","textEn":"Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects."},{"id":"a009-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「尺寸與危害」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate size and hazard?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同尺寸的不同污染物未必有相同電性影響。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Equal-sized contaminants can have different electrical effects. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-02"],"title":"粒子與分子","titleEn":"Distinguish particles and molecules","objective":"完成「粒子與分子」的敏感度草圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for distinguish particles and molecules, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：粒子與分子。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Distinguish particles and molecules. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「粒子與分子」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for distinguish particles and molecules and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「粒子與分子」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for distinguish particles and molecules: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-03-k1","title":"粒子與分子的原理","titleEn":"Distinguish particles and molecules principle","text":"粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。","textEn":"Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control."},{"id":"a009-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「粒子與分子」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating distinguish particles and molecules?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"粒子過濾不能自動證明分子污染受控。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Particle filtration does not establish molecular-contamination control. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-03"],"title":"暴露劑量","titleEn":"Estimate contamination exposure","objective":"完成「暴露劑量」的故障判別表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for estimate contamination exposure, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：暴露劑量。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂暴露模型：先假設沉積通量與濃度成正比。案例甲濃度 2、時間 3，案例乙濃度 1、時間 8；比較相對暴露，再列使此線性模型失效的吸附飽和情況。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate contamination exposure. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical exposure model: deposition flux is proportional to concentration. Compare relative exposures for concentration/time pairs (2,3) and (1,8), then state how adsorption saturation could invalidate linearity.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「暴露劑量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate contamination exposure and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「暴露劑量」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for estimate contamination exposure: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-04-k1","title":"暴露劑量的原理","titleEn":"Estimate contamination exposure principle","text":"表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。","textEn":"Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration."},{"id":"a009-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「暴露劑量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate contamination exposure?","options":["表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。","粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration.","Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面負荷同時取決於濃度與暴露時間。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Surface burden depends on concentration and exposure duration. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-04"],"title":"沉積與再懸浮","titleEn":"Trace deposition and resuspension","objective":"完成「沉積與再懸浮」的量測規劃，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for trace deposition and resuspension, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：沉積與再懸浮。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace deposition and resuspension. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「沉積與再懸浮」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace deposition and resuspension and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「沉積與再懸浮」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for trace deposition and resuspension: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-05-k1","title":"沉積與再懸浮的原理","titleEn":"Trace deposition and resuspension principle","text":"清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。","textEn":"Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles."},{"id":"a009-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「沉積與再懸浮」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace deposition and resuspension?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔表面的擾動可能重新釋出粒子。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Disturbing a surface can resuspend deposited particles. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}},{"id":"a009-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-05"],"title":"監控片安排","titleEn":"Choose monitoring wafers","objective":"完成「監控片安排」的工程驗收單，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for choose monitoring wafers, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：監控片安排。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose monitoring wafers. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Monitor wafers need representative handling histories. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Monitor wafers need representative handling histories. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。 應回到「監控片安排」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose monitoring wafers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「監控片安排」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for choose monitoring wafers: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-06-k1","title":"監控片安排的原理","titleEn":"Choose monitoring wafers principle","text":"監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。","textEn":"Monitor wafers need representative handling histories."},{"id":"a009-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","textEn":"Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「監控片安排」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose monitoring wafers?","options":["粒子數低就證明金屬離子濃度低。","未檢出代表污染濃度精確為零。","監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。"],"optionsEn":["Low particle counts prove low metal-ion concentration.","Nondetection means exactly zero contamination.","Monitor wafers need representative handling histories."],"answer":2,"explanation":"監控片需要與實際搬運歷程一致。 污染控制是來源、傳輸、表面沉積與器件敏感度的串聯問題；控制來源並不自動證明所有傳輸路徑已封閉。","explanationEn":"Monitor wafers need representative handling histories. Contamination links sources, transport, deposition and device sensitivity; source control does not prove all transport paths are closed."}}]},{"id":"a009-stage02","order":2,"title":"空氣與微環境","titleEn":"Air and microenvironments","description":"在「空氣與微環境」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for air and microenvironments, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a009-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-06"],"title":"氣流方向","titleEn":"Map airflow direction","objective":"完成「氣流方向」的因果圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map airflow direction, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氣流方向。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map airflow direction. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「氣流方向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map airflow direction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氣流方向」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map airflow direction: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-07-k1","title":"氣流方向的原理","titleEn":"Map airflow direction principle","text":"平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。","textEn":"Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation."},{"id":"a009-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氣流方向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map airflow direction?","options":["平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均風速無法取代局部回流辨識。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Mean velocity does not identify local recirculation. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-07"],"title":"濾材功能","titleEn":"Compare filter functions","objective":"完成「濾材功能」的對照表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare filter functions, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濾材功能。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare filter functions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「濾材功能」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare filter functions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濾材功能」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare filter functions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-08-k1","title":"濾材功能的原理","titleEn":"Compare filter functions principle","text":"粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。","textEn":"Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria."},{"id":"a009-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濾材功能」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare filter functions?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粒子濾材與分子吸附媒材的壽命判準不同。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Particle filters and molecular sorbents need different lifetime criteria. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-08"],"title":"壓差邊界","titleEn":"Set pressure-boundary evidence","objective":"完成「壓差邊界」的敏感度草圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for set pressure-boundary evidence, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：壓差邊界。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set pressure-boundary evidence. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「壓差邊界」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set pressure-boundary evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「壓差邊界」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for set pressure-boundary evidence: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-09-k1","title":"壓差邊界的原理","titleEn":"Set pressure-boundary evidence principle","text":"壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。","textEn":"Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport."},{"id":"a009-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「壓差邊界」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set pressure-boundary evidence?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壓差方向會影響污染跨區遷移。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Pressure gradients influence cross-zone contaminant transport. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-09"],"title":"微環境開口","titleEn":"Assess minienvironment openings","objective":"完成「微環境開口」的故障判別表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess minienvironment openings, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：微環境開口。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess minienvironment openings. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「微環境開口」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess minienvironment openings and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「微環境開口」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess minienvironment openings: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-10-k1","title":"微環境開口的原理","titleEn":"Assess minienvironment openings principle","text":"開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。","textEn":"Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure."},{"id":"a009-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「微環境開口」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess minienvironment openings?","options":["開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。","高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure.","High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"開口期間的短暫交換可能主導暴露。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Brief exchange during opening can dominate exposure. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-10"],"title":"FOUP 釋氣","titleEn":"Assess FOUP outgassing","objective":"完成「FOUP 釋氣」的量測規劃，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess foup outgassing, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：FOUP 釋氣。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess FOUP outgassing. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「FOUP 釋氣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess foup outgassing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「FOUP 釋氣」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess foup outgassing: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-11-k1","title":"FOUP 釋氣的原理","titleEn":"Assess FOUP outgassing principle","text":"載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。","textEn":"Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants."},{"id":"a009-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「FOUP 釋氣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess foup outgassing?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"載具材料可能儲存並釋出分子污染。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Carrier materials can store and release molecular contaminants. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}},{"id":"a009-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-11"],"title":"濕度耦合","titleEn":"Study humidity coupling","objective":"完成「濕度耦合」的工程驗收單，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for study humidity coupling, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濕度耦合。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Study humidity coupling. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。 應回到「濕度耦合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for study humidity coupling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濕度耦合」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for study humidity coupling: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-12-k1","title":"濕度耦合的原理","titleEn":"Study humidity coupling principle","text":"吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。","textEn":"Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity."},{"id":"a009-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","textEn":"Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濕度耦合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating study humidity coupling?","options":["高電阻率足以排除所有有機污染。","中央站合格即可省略使用點採樣。","吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。"],"optionsEn":["High resistivity rules out every organic contaminant.","Central-system acceptance eliminates point-of-use sampling.","Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"吸附與化學反應可能隨濕度改變。 粒子依慣性、擴散與重力等機制移動，分子污染則另受吸附平衡與化學反應影響。","explanationEn":"Adsorption and reactions can change with humidity. Particles move through inertia, diffusion and gravity, while molecular contamination also involves adsorption equilibria and reactions."}}]},{"id":"a009-stage03","order":3,"title":"液體接觸鏈","titleEn":"Liquid-contact chains","description":"在「液體接觸鏈」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for liquid-contact chains, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a009-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-12"],"title":"容器浸出物","titleEn":"Audit container extractables","objective":"完成「容器浸出物」的因果圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for audit container extractables, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：容器浸出物。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Audit container extractables. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「容器浸出物」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for audit container extractables and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「容器浸出物」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for audit container extractables: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-13-k1","title":"容器浸出物的原理","titleEn":"Audit container extractables principle","text":"化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。","textEn":"Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration."},{"id":"a009-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「容器浸出物」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating audit container extractables?","options":["化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"化學液潔淨度會受包材與接觸時間影響。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Chemical purity depends on packaging and contact duration. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-13"],"title":"管線顆粒脫落","titleEn":"Trace tubing particle shedding","objective":"完成「管線顆粒脫落」的對照表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace tubing particle shedding, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：管線顆粒脫落。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace tubing particle shedding. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「管線顆粒脫落」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace tubing particle shedding and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「管線顆粒脫落」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace tubing particle shedding: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-14-k1","title":"管線顆粒脫落的原理","titleEn":"Trace tubing particle shedding principle","text":"機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。","textEn":"Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding."},{"id":"a009-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「管線顆粒脫落」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace tubing particle shedding?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"機械擾動與維護可改變管線釋粒。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Mechanical disturbance and maintenance can change particle shedding. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-14"],"title":"閥件死腔","titleEn":"Locate valve dead volumes","objective":"完成「閥件死腔」的敏感度草圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for locate valve dead volumes, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閥件死腔。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate valve dead volumes. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「閥件死腔」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate valve dead volumes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閥件死腔」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for locate valve dead volumes: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-15-k1","title":"閥件死腔的原理","titleEn":"Locate valve dead volumes principle","text":"局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。","textEn":"Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels."},{"id":"a009-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閥件死腔」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate valve dead volumes?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部滯留可能使末端比主流更髒。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Stagnant valve volumes can contaminate outlets beyond bulk levels. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-15"],"title":"濾芯旁通","titleEn":"Check filtration bypass","objective":"完成「濾芯旁通」的故障判別表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for check filtration bypass, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濾芯旁通。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check filtration bypass. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「濾芯旁通」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check filtration bypass and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濾芯旁通」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for check filtration bypass: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-16-k1","title":"濾芯旁通的原理","titleEn":"Check filtration bypass principle","text":"濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。","textEn":"A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass."},{"id":"a009-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濾芯旁通」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check filtration bypass?","options":["濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。","濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass.","Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濾膜性能良好仍可能有密封失效旁通。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"A sound membrane can coexist with seal-related bypass. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-16"],"title":"靜電與吸附","titleEn":"Link electrostatics and attraction","objective":"完成「靜電與吸附」的量測規劃，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for link electrostatics and attraction, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：靜電與吸附。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Link electrostatics and attraction. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Charged surfaces can increase particle capture. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Charged surfaces can increase particle capture. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「靜電與吸附」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for link electrostatics and attraction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「靜電與吸附」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for link electrostatics and attraction: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-17-k1","title":"靜電與吸附的原理","titleEn":"Link electrostatics and attraction principle","text":"帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。","textEn":"Charged surfaces can increase particle capture."},{"id":"a009-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「靜電與吸附」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating link electrostatics and attraction?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Charged surfaces can increase particle capture.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface."],"answer":1,"explanation":"帶電表面可能增加粒子捕獲。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Charged surfaces can increase particle capture. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}},{"id":"a009-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-17"],"title":"化學批次更換","titleEn":"Compare chemical-lot transitions","objective":"完成「化學批次更換」的工程驗收單，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compare chemical-lot transitions, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：化學批次更換。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare chemical-lot transitions. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。 應回到「化學批次更換」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare chemical-lot transitions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「化學批次更換」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compare chemical-lot transitions: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-18-k1","title":"化學批次更換的原理","titleEn":"Compare chemical-lot transitions principle","text":"更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。","textEn":"Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages."},{"id":"a009-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","textEn":"Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「化學批次更換」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare chemical-lot transitions?","options":["濾膜截留尺寸等同所有污染物去除率。","加強清洗不可能改變基底表面。","更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Membrane retention size equals removal efficiency for every contaminant.","Stronger cleaning cannot change the substrate surface.","Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages."],"answer":2,"explanation":"更換批次的短暫尖峰可能被長時間平均掩蓋。 接液材料可能釋出原有污染或吸附後再釋放；材料名稱相同仍需比較潔淨處理與接觸歷史。","explanationEn":"Lot-transition spikes can disappear in long averages. Wetted materials can release inherent or previously adsorbed contamination; identical material names do not establish equal cleaning or contact histories."}}]},{"id":"a009-stage04","order":4,"title":"缺陷歸因","titleEn":"Defect attribution","description":"在「缺陷歸因」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for defect attribution, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a009-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-18"],"title":"檢出限標示","titleEn":"Report detection limits","objective":"完成「檢出限標示」的因果圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for report detection limits, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：檢出限標示。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Report detection limits. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「檢出限標示」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for report detection limits and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「檢出限標示」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for report detection limits: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-19-k1","title":"檢出限標示的原理","titleEn":"Report detection limits principle","text":"未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。","textEn":"Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination."},{"id":"a009-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「檢出限標示」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating report detection limits?","options":["未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未檢出不等於污染濃度嚴格為零。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Nondetection does not imply exactly zero contamination. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-19"],"title":"空間缺陷圖","titleEn":"Register defect maps","objective":"完成「空間缺陷圖」的對照表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for register defect maps, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：空間缺陷圖。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Register defect maps. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「空間缺陷圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for register defect maps and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「空間缺陷圖」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for register defect maps: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-20-k1","title":"空間缺陷圖的原理","titleEn":"Register defect maps principle","text":"缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。","textEn":"Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration."},{"id":"a009-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「空間缺陷圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating register defect maps?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺陷位置須與設備座標及晶圓旋轉對齊。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Defect maps need tool-coordinate and wafer-rotation registration. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-20"],"title":"時間序列比對","titleEn":"Align event timelines","objective":"完成「時間序列比對」的敏感度草圖，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for align event timelines, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：時間序列比對。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Align event timelines. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「時間序列比對」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for align event timelines and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「時間序列比對」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for align event timelines: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-21-k1","title":"時間序列比對的原理","titleEn":"Align event timelines principle","text":"維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。","textEn":"Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock."},{"id":"a009-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「時間序列比對」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating align event timelines?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock."],"answer":2,"explanation":"維護、換料及缺陷資料需要同一時間基準。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Maintenance, material changes and defects need a shared clock. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-21"],"title":"單因素隔離","titleEn":"Isolate a contamination hypothesis","objective":"完成「單因素隔離」的故障判別表，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for isolate a contamination hypothesis, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：單因素隔離。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Isolate a contamination hypothesis. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「單因素隔離」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for isolate a contamination hypothesis and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「單因素隔離」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for isolate a contamination hypothesis: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-22-k1","title":"單因素隔離的原理","titleEn":"Isolate a contamination hypothesis principle","text":"同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。","textEn":"Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution."},{"id":"a009-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「單因素隔離」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating isolate a contamination hypothesis?","options":["同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。","低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution.","Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時換多個零件會使因果歸因困難。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Replacing many components together obscures causal attribution. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-22"],"title":"恢復與放行","titleEn":"Define recovery evidence","objective":"完成「恢復與放行」的量測規劃，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define recovery evidence, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：恢復與放行。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define recovery evidence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「恢復與放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define recovery evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「恢復與放行」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define recovery evidence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-23-k1","title":"恢復與放行的原理","titleEn":"Define recovery evidence principle","text":"恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。","textEn":"Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms."},{"id":"a009-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「恢復與放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define recovery evidence?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination."],"answer":1,"explanation":"恢復背景須用獨立見證而不是只消除警報。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Recovery needs independent witnesses, not merely cleared alarms. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}},{"id":"a009-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-contam","v8a-purity","v8a-clean"],"prerequisiteIds":["a009-v8-23"],"title":"污染控制報告","titleEn":"Compile the control dossier","objective":"完成「污染控制報告」的工程驗收單，把來源、傳輸與缺陷地圖中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compile the control dossier, connecting relevant limits in sources, transport and defect maps to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：污染控制報告。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compile the control dossier. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。 應回到「污染控制報告」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compile the control dossier and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「污染控制報告」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compile the control dossier: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a009-v8-24-k1","title":"污染控制報告的原理","titleEn":"Compile the control dossier principle","text":"來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。","textEn":"Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately."},{"id":"a009-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","textEn":"A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「污染控制報告」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compile the control dossier?","options":["低壓差證明濾芯不存在任何旁通。","清洗後等待時間不影響再污染。","來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure drop proves no filtration bypass exists.","Queue time after cleaning cannot affect recontamination.","Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"來源、傳輸、沉積與電性後果應分層呈現。 一個缺陷熱點可由局部來源或流場集中造成；排查須把空間分布與事件時間線一起對照。","explanationEn":"Report source, transport, deposition and electrical consequence separately. A defect hotspot can reflect a local source or flow concentration; compare spatial patterns with event timelines."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"a010","title":"晶圓廠自動搬運系統","titleEn":"Automated material handling in fabs","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam","v3-media-80679a241086"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["搬運圖與產能","任務與交握","壅塞及故障","驗收與資料"],"labelsEn":["Transport graph and capacity","Tasks and handshakes","Congestion and faults","Acceptance and data"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a010-stage01","order":1,"title":"搬運圖與產能","titleEn":"Transport graph and capacity","description":"在「搬運圖與產能」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for transport graph and capacity, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a010-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"辨識載具與批號","titleEn":"Identify carriers and lots","objective":"完成「辨識載具與批號」的因果圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for identify carriers and lots, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：辨識載具與批號。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify carriers and lots. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「辨識載具與批號」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify carriers and lots and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「辨識載具與批號」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for identify carriers and lots: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-01-k1","title":"辨識載具與批號的原理","titleEn":"Identify carriers and lots principle","text":"載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。","textEn":"Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields."},{"id":"a010-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「辨識載具與批號」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify carriers and lots?","options":["載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。","平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。"],"optionsEn":["Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields.","Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"載具 ID 與晶圓批號不是同一資料欄位。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Carrier identity and wafer-lot identity are separate fields. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-01"],"title":"建立有向路網","titleEn":"Build the directed route graph","objective":"完成「建立有向路網」的對照表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for build the directed route graph, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：建立有向路網。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build the directed route graph. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「建立有向路網」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build the directed route graph and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「建立有向路網」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for build the directed route graph: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-02-k1","title":"建立有向路網的原理","titleEn":"Build the directed route graph principle","text":"單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。","textEn":"Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance."},{"id":"a010-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「建立有向路網」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build the directed route graph?","options":["平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。"],"optionsEn":["Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單向軌道的可達性不能由直線距離判斷。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Reachability on directed tracks differs from straight-line distance. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-02"],"title":"工具負載埠","titleEn":"Represent load ports","objective":"完成「工具負載埠」的敏感度草圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for represent load ports, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：工具負載埠。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Represent load ports. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「工具負載埠」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for represent load ports and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「工具負載埠」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for represent load ports: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-03-k1","title":"工具負載埠的原理","titleEn":"Represent load ports principle","text":"設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。","textEn":"Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models."},{"id":"a010-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「工具負載埠」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating represent load ports?","options":["平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。","設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。"],"optionsEn":["Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved.","Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設備加工能力與載入埠容量需分開建模。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Process capacity and load-port capacity require separate models. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-03"],"title":"搬運需求矩陣","titleEn":"Build a transport-demand matrix","objective":"完成「搬運需求矩陣」的故障判別表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for build a transport-demand matrix, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運需求矩陣。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a transport-demand matrix. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「搬運需求矩陣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a transport-demand matrix and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運需求矩陣」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for build a transport-demand matrix: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-04-k1","title":"搬運需求矩陣的原理","titleEn":"Build a transport-demand matrix principle","text":"製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。","textEn":"Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line."},{"id":"a010-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運需求矩陣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a transport-demand matrix?","options":["製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。","平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。"],"optionsEn":["Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line.","Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"製程回訪使晶圓不是只走一次單向流水線。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Reentrant processing makes wafer flow more than one pass down a line. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-04"],"title":"儲位與緩衝","titleEn":"Allocate storage buffers","objective":"完成「儲位與緩衝」的量測規劃，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for allocate storage buffers, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：儲位與緩衝。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Allocate storage buffers. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「儲位與緩衝」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for allocate storage buffers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「儲位與緩衝」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for allocate storage buffers: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-05-k1","title":"儲位與緩衝的原理","titleEn":"Allocate storage buffers principle","text":"緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。","textEn":"Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting."},{"id":"a010-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「儲位與緩衝」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating allocate storage buffers?","options":["平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。"],"optionsEn":["Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved."],"answer":1,"explanation":"緩衝減少阻塞但增加在製品與等待。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Buffers reduce blocking but increase work in process and waiting. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}},{"id":"a010-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-05"],"title":"搬運時間拆解","titleEn":"Decompose transport time","objective":"完成「搬運時間拆解」的工程驗收單，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for decompose transport time, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運時間拆解。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Decompose transport time. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。 應回到「搬運時間拆解」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task. Revisit assumptions and sampling for decompose transport time and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運時間拆解」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for decompose transport time: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-06-k1","title":"搬運時間拆解的原理","titleEn":"Decompose transport time principle","text":"等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。","textEn":"Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies."},{"id":"a010-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","textEn":"Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運時間拆解」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating decompose transport time?","options":["平均車速較快就保證所有任務延遲下降。","交握超時就代表載具尚未移動。","等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。"],"optionsEn":["Higher mean speed guarantees lower delay for every task.","Handshake timeout means the carrier has not moved.","Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"等待、行車、升降與交握各有不同改善途徑。 晶圓製程會反覆回到同類設備，搬運需求因此是有回路的網路問題，而非單向生產線的距離最小化。","explanationEn":"Queueing, travel, hoisting and handshakes need different remedies. Wafers revisit equipment types, making transport a reentrant network problem rather than one-way line-distance minimization."}}]},{"id":"a010-stage02","order":2,"title":"任務與交握","titleEn":"Tasks and handshakes","description":"在「任務與交握」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for tasks and handshakes, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a010-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-06"],"title":"任務狀態機","titleEn":"Draw the task state machine","objective":"完成「任務狀態機」的因果圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for draw the task state machine, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：任務狀態機。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw the task state machine. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「任務狀態機」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw the task state machine and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「任務狀態機」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for draw the task state machine: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-07-k1","title":"任務狀態機的原理","titleEn":"Draw the task state machine principle","text":"已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。","textEn":"Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states."},{"id":"a010-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「任務狀態機」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw the task state machine?","options":["已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。","任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states.","Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock."],"answer":0,"explanation":"已派工、已取貨與已送達不可合併為一個狀態。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Assigned, picked and delivered are distinct states. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-07"],"title":"載入前交握","titleEn":"Validate the loading handshake","objective":"完成「載入前交握」的對照表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for validate the loading handshake, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：載入前交握。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Validate the loading handshake. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「載入前交握」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for validate the loading handshake and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「載入前交握」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for validate the loading handshake: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-08-k1","title":"載入前交握的原理","titleEn":"Validate the loading handshake principle","text":"設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。","textEn":"Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity."},{"id":"a010-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「載入前交握」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating validate the loading handshake?","options":["任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock."],"answer":1,"explanation":"設備就緒與載具身分均需確認才可完成交接。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Handoff requires both equipment readiness and carrier identity. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-08"],"title":"路段保留","titleEn":"Reserve track segments","objective":"完成「路段保留」的敏感度草圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for reserve track segments, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：路段保留。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Reserve track segments. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「路段保留」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for reserve track segments and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「路段保留」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for reserve track segments: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-09-k1","title":"路段保留的原理","titleEn":"Reserve track segments principle","text":"避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。","textEn":"Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing."},{"id":"a010-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「路段保留」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating reserve track segments?","options":["任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。","避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock.","Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"避免碰撞需要互斥資源，不只是最短路徑。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Collision avoidance needs exclusive resources beyond shortest routing. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-09"],"title":"優先權與飢餓","titleEn":"Balance priority and starvation","objective":"完成「優先權與飢餓」的故障判別表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for balance priority and starvation, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：優先權與飢餓。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Balance priority and starvation. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「優先權與飢餓」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for balance priority and starvation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「優先權與飢餓」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for balance priority and starvation: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-10-k1","title":"優先權與飢餓的原理","titleEn":"Balance priority and starvation principle","text":"高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。","textEn":"High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots."},{"id":"a010-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「優先權與飢餓」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating balance priority and starvation?","options":["高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。","任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。"],"optionsEn":["High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots.","Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高優先任務不應無限阻斷普通批次。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"High-priority tasks should not indefinitely starve ordinary lots. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-10"],"title":"重試冪等性","titleEn":"Make retries idempotent","objective":"完成「重試冪等性」的量測規劃，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for make retries idempotent, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：重試冪等性。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Make retries idempotent. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「重試冪等性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for make retries idempotent and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「重試冪等性」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for make retries idempotent: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-11-k1","title":"重試冪等性的原理","titleEn":"Make retries idempotent principle","text":"重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。","textEn":"Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks."},{"id":"a010-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「重試冪等性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating make retries idempotent?","options":["任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。"],"optionsEn":["Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重送訊息不能產生第二個實體取貨任務。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Repeated messages must not create duplicate physical pickup tasks. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}},{"id":"a010-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-11"],"title":"超時狀態","titleEn":"Handle timeout ambiguity","objective":"完成「超時狀態」的工程驗收單，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for handle timeout ambiguity, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：超時狀態。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Handle timeout ambiguity. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。 應回到「超時狀態」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for handle timeout ambiguity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「超時狀態」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for handle timeout ambiguity: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-12-k1","title":"超時狀態的原理","titleEn":"Handle timeout ambiguity principle","text":"超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。","textEn":"Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action."},{"id":"a010-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","textEn":"Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「超時狀態」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating handle timeout ambiguity?","options":["任務重試可以建立新的實體取貨而不核對狀態。","最短路徑自動保證沒有資源死鎖。","超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。"],"optionsEn":["Retries can start another pickup without state reconciliation.","Shortest paths automatically prevent resource deadlock.","Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action."],"answer":2,"explanation":"超時可能是訊息遺失而不是動作未發生。 物理移動與資訊確認可能不同步；任務識別碼及冪等重試能避免遺失回覆導致重複搬運。","explanationEn":"Timeout may mean lost acknowledgement rather than no action. Physical movement and acknowledgement may differ in time; unique task IDs and idempotent retries prevent duplicate transport after lost replies."}}]},{"id":"a010-stage03","order":3,"title":"壅塞及故障","titleEn":"Congestion and faults","description":"在「壅塞及故障」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for congestion and faults, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a010-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-12"],"title":"瓶頸利用率","titleEn":"Measure bottleneck utilization","objective":"完成「瓶頸利用率」的因果圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for measure bottleneck utilization, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：瓶頸利用率。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure bottleneck utilization. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「瓶頸利用率」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure bottleneck utilization and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「瓶頸利用率」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for measure bottleneck utilization: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-13-k1","title":"瓶頸利用率的原理","titleEn":"Measure bottleneck utilization principle","text":"高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。","textEn":"High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment."},{"id":"a010-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「瓶頸利用率」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure bottleneck utilization?","options":["高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。","已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。"],"optionsEn":["High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment.","Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高平均車速不能證明最繁忙路段不塞車。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"High average speed does not exclude congestion on a busy segment. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-13"],"title":"路口壅塞","titleEn":"Inspect junction queues","objective":"完成「路口壅塞」的對照表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for inspect junction queues, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：路口壅塞。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect junction queues. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Junction service limits propagate queues upstream. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Junction service limits propagate queues upstream. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「路口壅塞」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect junction queues and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「路口壅塞」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for inspect junction queues: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-14-k1","title":"路口壅塞的原理","titleEn":"Inspect junction queues principle","text":"合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。","textEn":"Junction service limits propagate queues upstream."},{"id":"a010-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「路口壅塞」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect junction queues?","options":["已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Junction service limits propagate queues upstream.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"合流點服務率限制會擴散到上游路段。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"Junction service limits propagate queues upstream. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-14"],"title":"故障車阻擋","titleEn":"Model a blocked vehicle","objective":"完成「故障車阻擋」的敏感度草圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for model a blocked vehicle, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：故障車阻擋。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Model a blocked vehicle. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「故障車阻擋」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for model a blocked vehicle and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「故障車阻擋」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for model a blocked vehicle: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-15-k1","title":"故障車阻擋的原理","titleEn":"Model a blocked vehicle principle","text":"停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。","textEn":"A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability."},{"id":"a010-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「故障車阻擋」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating model a blocked vehicle?","options":["已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。","停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks.","A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"停在單線區的故障車可改變整個路網可達性。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"A failed vehicle on a single lane can change network reachability. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-15"],"title":"負載埠拒收","titleEn":"Recover from port rejection","objective":"完成「負載埠拒收」的故障判別表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for recover from port rejection, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：負載埠拒收。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Recover from port rejection. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「負載埠拒收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for recover from port rejection and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「負載埠拒收」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for recover from port rejection: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-16-k1","title":"負載埠拒收的原理","titleEn":"Recover from port rejection principle","text":"目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。","textEn":"Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task."},{"id":"a010-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「負載埠拒收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating recover from port rejection?","options":["目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。","已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。"],"optionsEn":["Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task.","Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"目的端拒收需要可追溯的回退任務。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"Destination rejection requires a traceable fallback task. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-16"],"title":"掉線與恢復","titleEn":"Reconcile network recovery","objective":"完成「掉線與恢復」的量測規劃，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for reconcile network recovery, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：掉線與恢復。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Reconcile network recovery. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「掉線與恢復」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for reconcile network recovery and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「掉線與恢復」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for reconcile network recovery: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-17-k1","title":"掉線與恢復的原理","titleEn":"Reconcile network recovery principle","text":"恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。","textEn":"Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states."},{"id":"a010-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「掉線與恢復」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating reconcile network recovery?","options":["已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"恢復時要核對實體位置與系統任務狀態。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"Recovery must reconcile physical locations with task states. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}},{"id":"a010-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-17"],"title":"地震或急停","titleEn":"Model emergency-stop states","objective":"完成「地震或急停」的工程驗收單，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for model emergency-stop states, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：地震或急停。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Model emergency-stop states. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。 應回到「地震或急停」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Assigned and delivered can share one state. Revisit assumptions and sampling for model emergency-stop states and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「地震或急停」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for model emergency-stop states: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-18-k1","title":"地震或急停的原理","titleEn":"Model emergency-stop states principle","text":"安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。","textEn":"Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation."},{"id":"a010-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","textEn":"Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「地震或急停」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating model emergency-stop states?","options":["已派工與已送達可使用同一狀態。","只需驗證產能，不必量測搬運潔淨度。","安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。"],"optionsEn":["Assigned and delivered can share one state.","Throughput alone suffices without transport cleanliness checks.","Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"安全停機後的重啟不能沿用未核對的任務。 路段利用率接近滿載時，微小到達波動可能形成長隊列；提高全廠平均車速不一定解除局部合流瓶頸。","explanationEn":"Restart after a safety stop needs task reconciliation. Near-capacity segments can develop long queues under small arrival variations; faster average travel may not resolve a local merging bottleneck."}}]},{"id":"a010-stage04","order":4,"title":"驗收與資料","titleEn":"Acceptance and data","description":"在「驗收與資料」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for acceptance and data, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a010-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-18"],"title":"搬運振動","titleEn":"Assess transport vibration","objective":"完成「搬運振動」的因果圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess transport vibration, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運振動。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess transport vibration. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「搬運振動」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess transport vibration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運振動」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess transport vibration: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-19-k1","title":"搬運振動的原理","titleEn":"Assess transport vibration principle","text":"峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。","textEn":"Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads."},{"id":"a010-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運振動」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess transport vibration?","options":["峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。","中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。"],"optionsEn":["Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads.","An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"峰值加速度與振動頻譜都可能影響脆弱載荷。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Peak acceleration and vibration spectra can affect fragile payloads. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-19"],"title":"粒子增量","titleEn":"Measure transport particle adders","objective":"完成「粒子增量」的對照表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure transport particle adders, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：粒子增量。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure transport particle adders. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「粒子增量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure transport particle adders and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「粒子增量」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure transport particle adders: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-20-k1","title":"粒子增量的原理","titleEn":"Measure transport particle adders principle","text":"潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。","textEn":"Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories."},{"id":"a010-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「粒子增量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure transport particle adders?","options":["中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"潔淨搬運需比較匹配歷程的前後監控片。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Clean transport requires matched before-after monitor histories. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-20"],"title":"尾端延遲","titleEn":"Report tail latency","objective":"完成「尾端延遲」的敏感度草圖，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for report tail latency, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：尾端延遲。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂延遲資料：九次任務均 20 s，一次 200 s；計算平均與中位數，保留最大值，再設計會揭露尾端問題的報表欄位。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Report tail latency. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical latency data: nine tasks take 20 s and one takes 200 s. Compute mean and median, retain the maximum, and design a report exposing tail delays.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「尾端延遲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for report tail latency and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「尾端延遲」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for report tail latency: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-21-k1","title":"尾端延遲的原理","titleEn":"Report tail latency principle","text":"中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。","textEn":"Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays."},{"id":"a010-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「尾端延遲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating report tail latency?","options":["中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。","中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions.","Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays."],"answer":2,"explanation":"中位搬運時間可能掩蓋少數嚴重逾時。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Median transfer time can hide severe tail delays. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-21"],"title":"事件追溯","titleEn":"Audit event traceability","objective":"完成「事件追溯」的故障判別表，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for audit event traceability, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：事件追溯。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Audit event traceability. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「事件追溯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for audit event traceability and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「事件追溯」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for audit event traceability: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-22-k1","title":"事件追溯的原理","titleEn":"Audit event traceability principle","text":"每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。","textEn":"Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity."},{"id":"a010-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「事件追溯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating audit event traceability?","options":["每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。","中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。"],"optionsEn":["Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity.","An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每個交接事件應保留來源、時間與唯一任務 ID。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Each handoff needs source, time and unique task identity. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-22"],"title":"離散事件模擬","titleEn":"Build a discrete-event experiment","objective":"完成「離散事件模擬」的量測規劃，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for build a discrete-event experiment, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：離散事件模擬。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Build a discrete-event experiment. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「離散事件模擬」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for build a discrete-event experiment and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「離散事件模擬」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for build a discrete-event experiment: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-23-k1","title":"離散事件模擬的原理","titleEn":"Build a discrete-event experiment principle","text":"相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。","textEn":"Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison."},{"id":"a010-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「離散事件模擬」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating build a discrete-event experiment?","options":["中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同到達序列才能公平比較不同派工策略。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Dispatch strategies need identical arrival traces for fair comparison. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}},{"id":"a010-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-amhs","v8a-daifuku","v8a-contam"],"prerequisiteIds":["a010-v8-23"],"title":"搬運系統驗收","titleEn":"Accept the transport system","objective":"完成「搬運系統驗收」的工程驗收單，把載具交握、尾端延遲、故障恢復中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept the transport system, connecting relevant limits in carrier handshakes, tail latency and recovery to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：搬運系統驗收。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept the transport system. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。 應回到「搬運系統驗收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept the transport system and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「搬運系統驗收」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept the transport system: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a010-v8-24-k1","title":"搬運系統驗收的原理","titleEn":"Accept the transport system principle","text":"產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。","textEn":"Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence."},{"id":"a010-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","textEn":"Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「搬運系統驗收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept the transport system?","options":["中位延遲合格就不會有嚴重逾時。","系統重啟可以跳過實體位置核對。","產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable median excludes severe timeouts.","Restart can skip verification of physical positions.","Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"產能、錯送防護、故障恢復及潔淨度均需證據。 設備吞吐量、尾端等待、錯送率、振動與污染是不同驗收維度，必須在同一代表性工作負載下比較。","explanationEn":"Acceptance needs throughput, misdelivery prevention, recovery and cleanliness evidence. Throughput, tail waits, misdelivery, vibration and contamination are distinct acceptance dimensions needing the same representative workload."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"a011","title":"熱氧化閘極介電層","titleEn":"Thermally grown gate dielectrics","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["界面與氧化目的","成長動力學","厚度與電性","元件熱整合"],"labelsEn":["Interface and oxidation purpose","Growth kinetics","Thickness and electrical evidence","Device thermal integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a011-stage01","order":1,"title":"界面與氧化目的","titleEn":"Interface and oxidation purpose","description":"在「界面與氧化目的」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for interface and oxidation purpose, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a011-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"分辨成長與沉積","titleEn":"Separate growth and deposition","objective":"完成「分辨成長與沉積」的因果圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate growth and deposition, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：分辨成長與沉積。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate growth and deposition. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「分辨成長與沉積」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate growth and deposition and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「分辨成長與沉積」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate growth and deposition: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-01-k1","title":"分辨成長與沉積的原理","titleEn":"Separate growth and deposition principle","text":"熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。","textEn":"Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source."},{"id":"a011-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「分辨成長與沉積」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate growth and deposition?","options":["熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱氧化消耗基板矽，外加沉積的材料來源不同。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Thermal oxidation consumes substrate silicon; deposition has another material source. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-01"],"title":"界面位置移動","titleEn":"Track the moving interface","objective":"完成「界面位置移動」的對照表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for track the moving interface, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界面位置移動。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂幾何模型：假設氧化物厚度 100 個單位、矽消耗為其 0.44 倍；以原表面為零畫出新界面與外表面。0.44 是近似體積換算，非本課量測值。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track the moving interface. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical geometry: oxide thickness 100 units and silicon consumption 0.44 times that thickness. Mark the new interface and outer surface relative to the original surface. The 0.44 is an approximate volume conversion, not course measurement data.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「界面位置移動」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track the moving interface and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界面位置移動」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for track the moving interface: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-02-k1","title":"界面位置移動的原理","titleEn":"Track the moving interface principle","text":"氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。","textEn":"The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface."},{"id":"a011-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界面位置移動」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track the moving interface?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"氧化後原表面不等於新的矽氧界面位置。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"The original surface differs from the final silicon-oxide interface. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-02"],"title":"閘氧與場氧","titleEn":"Separate gate and field oxide","objective":"完成「閘氧與場氧」的敏感度草圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate gate and field oxide, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘氧與場氧。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate gate and field oxide. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閘氧與場氧」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate gate and field oxide and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘氧與場氧」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate gate and field oxide: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-03-k1","title":"閘氧與場氧的原理","titleEn":"Separate gate and field oxide principle","text":"電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。","textEn":"Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets."},{"id":"a011-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘氧與場氧」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate gate and field oxide?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電容控制與區域隔離使用不同設計目標。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Gate capacitance and field isolation have different design targets. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-03"],"title":"乾氧與濕氧","titleEn":"Compare dry and wet oxidation","objective":"完成「乾氧與濕氧」的故障判別表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare dry and wet oxidation, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：乾氧與濕氧。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare dry and wet oxidation. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「乾氧與濕氧」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare dry and wet oxidation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「乾氧與濕氧」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare dry and wet oxidation: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-04-k1","title":"乾氧與濕氧的原理","titleEn":"Compare dry and wet oxidation principle","text":"氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。","textEn":"Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties."},{"id":"a011-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「乾氧與濕氧」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare dry and wet oxidation?","options":["氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"氧化氣氛改變成長速率及薄膜特性。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Oxidizing ambient changes growth kinetics and film properties. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-04"],"title":"原生氧化前史","titleEn":"Record initial oxide history","objective":"完成「原生氧化前史」的量測規劃，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for record initial oxide history, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：原生氧化前史。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Record initial oxide history. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「原生氧化前史」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for record initial oxide history and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「原生氧化前史」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for record initial oxide history: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-05-k1","title":"原生氧化前史的原理","titleEn":"Record initial oxide history principle","text":"初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。","textEn":"Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth."},{"id":"a011-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「原生氧化前史」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating record initial oxide history?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始氧化層會改變短時間成長的起點。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Initial oxide changes the starting condition for short growth. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}},{"id":"a011-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-05"],"title":"清洗後等待","titleEn":"Assess the clean-to-oxidation delay","objective":"完成「清洗後等待」的工程驗收單，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess the clean-to-oxidation delay, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：清洗後等待。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess the clean-to-oxidation delay. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「清洗後等待」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess the clean-to-oxidation delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「清洗後等待」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess the clean-to-oxidation delay: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-06-k1","title":"清洗後等待的原理","titleEn":"Assess the clean-to-oxidation delay principle","text":"吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。","textEn":"Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface."},{"id":"a011-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","textEn":"Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「清洗後等待」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess the clean-to-oxidation delay?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"吸附與再氧化會改變最初界面。 熱氧化形成的氧化物同時向原表面上下延伸；截面預算需分開記錄矽消耗與外部厚度增加。","explanationEn":"Adsorption and reoxidation change the starting interface. Thermal oxide extends above and below the original surface; separate silicon consumption from outward thickness increase."}}]},{"id":"a011-stage02","order":2,"title":"成長動力學","titleEn":"Growth kinetics","description":"在「成長動力學」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for growth kinetics, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a011-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-06"],"title":"線性成長區","titleEn":"Identify the linear regime","objective":"完成「線性成長區」的因果圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for identify the linear regime, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：線性成長區。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify the linear regime. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「線性成長區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify the linear regime and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「線性成長區」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for identify the linear regime: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-07-k1","title":"線性成長區的原理","titleEn":"Identify the linear regime principle","text":"薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。","textEn":"Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited."},{"id":"a011-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「線性成長區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify the linear regime?","options":["薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄層成長可能主要受界面反應限制。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Thin-film growth can be mainly interface-reaction limited. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-07"],"title":"拋物線成長區","titleEn":"Identify the parabolic regime","objective":"完成「拋物線成長區」的對照表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for identify the parabolic regime, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：拋物線成長區。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify the parabolic regime. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「拋物線成長區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify the parabolic regime and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「拋物線成長區」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for identify the parabolic regime: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-08-k1","title":"拋物線成長區的原理","titleEn":"Identify the parabolic regime principle","text":"厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。","textEn":"Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide."},{"id":"a011-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「拋物線成長區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify the parabolic regime?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚氧化層增加氧化物穿越的傳輸阻力。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Thicker oxide increases transport resistance through the oxide. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-08"],"title":"模型初始條件","titleEn":"Set model initial conditions","objective":"完成「模型初始條件」的敏感度草圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for set model initial conditions, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：模型初始條件。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set model initial conditions. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「模型初始條件」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set model initial conditions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「模型初始條件」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for set model initial conditions: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-09-k1","title":"模型初始條件的原理","titleEn":"Set model initial conditions principle","text":"套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。","textEn":"Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition."},{"id":"a011-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「模型初始條件」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set model initial conditions?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"套用成長模型需帶入原有膜厚而非從零開始。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Growth models need the existing thickness as an initial condition. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-09"],"title":"晶向效應","titleEn":"Assess orientation effects","objective":"完成「晶向效應」的故障判別表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess orientation effects, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶向效應。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess orientation effects. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「晶向效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess orientation effects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶向效應」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess orientation effects: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-10-k1","title":"晶向效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess orientation effects principle","text":"不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。","textEn":"Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates."},{"id":"a011-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶向效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess orientation effects?","options":["不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同矽晶面可能呈現不同界面反應速率。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Different silicon planes can have different interface reaction rates. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-10"],"title":"摻雜效應","titleEn":"Assess doping effects","objective":"完成「摻雜效應」的量測規劃，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess doping effects, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：摻雜效應。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess doping effects. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「摻雜效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess doping effects and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「摻雜效應」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess doping effects: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-11-k1","title":"摻雜效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess doping effects principle","text":"重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。","textEn":"Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves."},{"id":"a011-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「摻雜效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess doping effects?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重摻雜區與未摻雜區不能直接共用同一成長曲線。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Heavily doped and undoped regions need not share growth curves. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}},{"id":"a011-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-11"],"title":"應力耦合","titleEn":"Trace oxidation stress","objective":"完成「應力耦合」的工程驗收單，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for trace oxidation stress, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應力耦合。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace oxidation stress. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「應力耦合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace oxidation stress and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「應力耦合」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for trace oxidation stress: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-12-k1","title":"應力耦合的原理","titleEn":"Trace oxidation stress principle","text":"氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。","textEn":"Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress."},{"id":"a011-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","textEn":"Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「應力耦合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace oxidation stress?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"氧化體積變化與周邊拘束共同形成應力。 Deal–Grove 型關係把界面反應與氧化劑穿越氧化層的傳輸串接；極薄層需另檢查模型偏差。","explanationEn":"Oxidation volume change and surrounding constraints generate stress. Deal–Grove-type relations combine interface reaction and oxidant transport through oxide; ultrathin films require additional model checks."}}]},{"id":"a011-stage03","order":3,"title":"厚度與電性","titleEn":"Thickness and electrical evidence","description":"在「厚度與電性」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for thickness and electrical evidence, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a011-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-12"],"title":"橢偏膜厚","titleEn":"Interpret ellipsometric thickness","objective":"完成「橢偏膜厚」的因果圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for interpret ellipsometric thickness, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：橢偏膜厚。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret ellipsometric thickness. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「橢偏膜厚」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret ellipsometric thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「橢偏膜厚」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for interpret ellipsometric thickness: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-13-k1","title":"橢偏膜厚的原理","titleEn":"Interpret ellipsometric thickness principle","text":"光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。","textEn":"Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions."},{"id":"a011-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「橢偏膜厚」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret ellipsometric thickness?","options":["光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光學膜厚反演需要折射率與堆疊假設。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"Optical thickness extraction requires index and stack assumptions. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-13"],"title":"截面校對","titleEn":"Cross-check section thickness","objective":"完成「截面校對」的對照表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for cross-check section thickness, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：截面校對。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Cross-check section thickness. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「截面校對」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for cross-check section thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「截面校對」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for cross-check section thickness: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-14-k1","title":"截面校對的原理","titleEn":"Cross-check section thickness principle","text":"局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。","textEn":"A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity."},{"id":"a011-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「截面校對」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating cross-check section thickness?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部截面可校核光學模型但不能代表整片。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"A local section checks optical models but not full-wafer uniformity. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-14"],"title":"電容等效厚度","titleEn":"Infer electrical thickness","objective":"完成「電容等效厚度」的敏感度草圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for infer electrical thickness, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：電容等效厚度。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Infer electrical thickness. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「電容等效厚度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for infer electrical thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「電容等效厚度」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for infer electrical thickness: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-15-k1","title":"電容等效厚度的原理","titleEn":"Infer electrical thickness principle","text":"介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。","textEn":"Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness."},{"id":"a011-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「電容等效厚度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating infer electrical thickness?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介面層與量子效應可能使電容厚度不同於物理厚度。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"Interfacial and quantum effects can separate electrical and physical thickness. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-15"],"title":"漏電曲線","titleEn":"Read leakage curves","objective":"完成「漏電曲線」的故障判別表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for read leakage curves, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：漏電曲線。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read leakage curves. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「漏電曲線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read leakage curves and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「漏電曲線」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for read leakage curves: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-16-k1","title":"漏電曲線的原理","titleEn":"Read leakage curves principle","text":"比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。","textEn":"Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity."},{"id":"a011-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「漏電曲線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read leakage curves?","options":["比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較漏電需控制面積、電場及量測極性。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"Leakage comparisons need matched area, field and polarity. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-16"],"title":"界面陷阱指標","titleEn":"Inspect interface-trap evidence","objective":"完成「界面陷阱指標」的量測規劃，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect interface-trap evidence, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：界面陷阱指標。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect interface-trap evidence. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「界面陷阱指標」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect interface-trap evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「界面陷阱指標」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect interface-trap evidence: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-17-k1","title":"界面陷阱指標的原理","titleEn":"Inspect interface-trap evidence principle","text":"C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。","textEn":"C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics."},{"id":"a011-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「界面陷阱指標」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect interface-trap evidence?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"C-V 頻率依賴可能含介面態與量測寄生影響。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"C-V frequency dependence can include interface states and measurement parasitics. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}},{"id":"a011-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-17"],"title":"擊穿分布","titleEn":"Analyze breakdown distributions","objective":"完成「擊穿分布」的工程驗收單，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for analyze breakdown distributions, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：擊穿分布。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Analyze breakdown distributions. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「擊穿分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for analyze breakdown distributions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「擊穿分布」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for analyze breakdown distributions: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-18-k1","title":"擊穿分布的原理","titleEn":"Analyze breakdown distributions principle","text":"單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。","textEn":"One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability."},{"id":"a011-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","textEn":"Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「擊穿分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating analyze breakdown distributions?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一最佳樣本不能代表批次可靠度。 電容量測反映電性有效堆疊，光學量測依賴折射率模型，兩者一致性可用來檢查介面層假設。","explanationEn":"One best specimen cannot represent lot reliability. Capacitance reflects an electrical stack while optical measurements depend on refractive-index models; agreement can test interfacial-layer assumptions."}}]},{"id":"a011-stage04","order":4,"title":"元件熱整合","titleEn":"Device thermal integration","description":"在「元件熱整合」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for device thermal integration, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a011-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-18"],"title":"熱預算累加","titleEn":"Accumulate thermal history","objective":"完成「熱預算累加」的因果圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for accumulate thermal history, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱預算累加。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accumulate thermal history. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「熱預算累加」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accumulate thermal history and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱預算累加」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for accumulate thermal history: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-19-k1","title":"熱預算累加的原理","titleEn":"Accumulate thermal history principle","text":"長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。","textEn":"Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles."},{"id":"a011-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱預算累加」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accumulate thermal history?","options":["長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"長時間氧化會同時改變先前的摻雜輪廓。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Long oxidation can also change earlier dopant profiles. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-19"],"title":"邊角氧化","titleEn":"Assess corner oxidation","objective":"完成「邊角氧化」的對照表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess corner oxidation, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊角氧化。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess corner oxidation. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「邊角氧化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess corner oxidation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊角氧化」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess corner oxidation: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-20-k1","title":"邊角氧化的原理","titleEn":"Assess corner oxidation principle","text":"二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。","textEn":"Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth."},{"id":"a011-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊角氧化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess corner oxidation?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"二維曲率與應力使角落成長不同於平面。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Two-dimensional curvature and stress alter corner growth. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-20"],"title":"固定電荷","titleEn":"Separate fixed charge","objective":"完成「固定電荷」的敏感度草圖，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate fixed charge, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：固定電荷。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate fixed charge. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「固定電荷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate fixed charge and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「固定電荷」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate fixed charge: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-21-k1","title":"固定電荷的原理","titleEn":"Separate fixed charge principle","text":"固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。","textEn":"Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences."},{"id":"a011-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「固定電荷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate fixed charge?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences."],"answer":2,"explanation":"固定電荷造成的電壓位移不等同於功函數差。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Fixed-charge voltage shifts differ from work-function differences. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-21"],"title":"氮化選項","titleEn":"Evaluate nitridation tradeoffs","objective":"完成「氮化選項」的故障判別表，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for evaluate nitridation tradeoffs, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氮化選項。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Evaluate nitridation tradeoffs. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「氮化選項」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for evaluate nitridation tradeoffs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氮化選項」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for evaluate nitridation tradeoffs: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-22-k1","title":"氮化選項的原理","titleEn":"Evaluate nitridation tradeoffs principle","text":"介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。","textEn":"Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together."},{"id":"a011-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氮化選項」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating evaluate nitridation tradeoffs?","options":["介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"介面工程必須同時評估漏電、陷阱與遷移率。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Interface engineering must consider leakage, traps and mobility together. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-22"],"title":"模型失效界線","titleEn":"State model limits","objective":"完成「模型失效界線」的量測規劃，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for state model limits, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：模型失效界線。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: State model limits. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「模型失效界線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for state model limits and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「模型失效界線」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for state model limits: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-23-k1","title":"模型失效界線的原理","titleEn":"State model limits principle","text":"經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。","textEn":"Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces."},{"id":"a011-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「模型失效界線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating state model limits?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"經典厚膜模型不能無條件外推到極薄介面。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Classical thick-film models cannot be unconditionally extrapolated to ultrathin interfaces. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}},{"id":"a011-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-oxide","v8a-mit","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a011-v8-23"],"title":"閘氧驗收","titleEn":"Accept the gate oxide","objective":"完成「閘氧驗收」的工程驗收單，把氧化消耗、界面陷阱、漏電中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept the gate oxide, connecting relevant limits in oxidation consumption, interface traps and leakage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘氧驗收。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept the gate oxide. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「閘氧驗收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept the gate oxide and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘氧驗收」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept the gate oxide: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a011-v8-24-k1","title":"閘氧驗收的原理","titleEn":"Accept the gate oxide principle","text":"厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。","textEn":"Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability."},{"id":"a011-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","textEn":"Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘氧驗收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept the gate oxide?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"厚度圖、介面、漏電與可靠度缺一不可。 氧化也消耗熱預算並改變摻雜輪廓，因此合格氧化層仍可能造成鄰近接面或短通道指標變差。","explanationEn":"Acceptance needs thickness mapping, interface quality, leakage and reliability. Oxidation consumes thermal budget and alters dopant profiles, so an acceptable oxide can coexist with degraded junction or short-channel behavior."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a012","title":"高介電常數原子層沉積","titleEn":"High-k atomic layer deposition","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["介電層與電容","表面循環","三維覆蓋","電性及整合"],"labelsEn":["Dielectric and capacitance","Surface cycles","Three-dimensional coverage","Electrical behavior and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a012-stage01","order":1,"title":"介電層與電容","titleEn":"Dielectric and capacitance","description":"在「介電層與電容」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for dielectric and capacitance, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a012-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"物理厚度與 EOT","titleEn":"Separate thickness and EOT","objective":"完成「物理厚度與 EOT」的因果圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate thickness and eot, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：物理厚度與 EOT。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate thickness and EOT. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「物理厚度與 EOT」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate thickness and eot and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「物理厚度與 EOT」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate thickness and eot: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-01-k1","title":"物理厚度與 EOT的原理","titleEn":"Separate thickness and EOT principle","text":"較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。","textEn":"Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance."},{"id":"a012-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「物理厚度與 EOT」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate thickness and eot?","options":["較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"較高介電常數可在相同電容下容許較厚物理膜。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Higher permittivity permits greater physical thickness at equal capacitance. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-01"],"title":"串聯介面電容","titleEn":"Calculate series interface capacitance","objective":"完成「串聯介面電容」的對照表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for calculate series interface capacitance, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：串聯介面電容。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂電容模型：令介面與上層電容分別為 2 與 8 個單位；算串聯總電容，再將上層增為 16。比較收益並說明瓶頸。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Calculate series interface capacitance. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical capacitance model: interface and upper-layer capacitances are 2 and 8 units. Calculate series capacitance, increase the upper layer to 16 and identify the limiting contribution.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「串聯介面電容」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for calculate series interface capacitance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「串聯介面電容」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for calculate series interface capacitance: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-02-k1","title":"串聯介面電容的原理","titleEn":"Calculate series interface capacitance principle","text":"薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。","textEn":"A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness."},{"id":"a012-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「串聯介面電容」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating calculate series interface capacitance?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄介面層仍可能主導整體等效氧化厚度。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"A thin interfacial layer can dominate equivalent oxide thickness. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-02"],"title":"基底終端基團","titleEn":"Identify surface termination","objective":"完成「基底終端基團」的敏感度草圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for identify surface termination, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：基底終端基團。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify surface termination. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「基底終端基團」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify surface termination and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「基底終端基團」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for identify surface termination: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-03-k1","title":"基底終端基團的原理","titleEn":"Identify surface termination principle","text":"表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。","textEn":"Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation."},{"id":"a012-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「基底終端基團」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify surface termination?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面官能基影響前驅物吸附與成核。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Surface functional groups affect precursor adsorption and nucleation. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-03"],"title":"前驅物相容性","titleEn":"Review precursor compatibility","objective":"完成「前驅物相容性」的故障判別表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for review precursor compatibility, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：前驅物相容性。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review precursor compatibility. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「前驅物相容性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review precursor compatibility and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「前驅物相容性」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for review precursor compatibility: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-04-k1","title":"前驅物相容性的原理","titleEn":"Review precursor compatibility principle","text":"揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。","textEn":"Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together."},{"id":"a012-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「前驅物相容性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review precursor compatibility?","options":["揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"揮發性、穩定性及殘留物需一起考慮。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Volatility, stability and residues must be considered together. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-04"],"title":"成核延遲","titleEn":"Measure nucleation delay","objective":"完成「成核延遲」的量測規劃，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for measure nucleation delay, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：成核延遲。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure nucleation delay. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「成核延遲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure nucleation delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「成核延遲」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for measure nucleation delay: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-05-k1","title":"成核延遲的原理","titleEn":"Measure nucleation delay principle","text":"最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。","textEn":"Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth."},{"id":"a012-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「成核延遲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure nucleation delay?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最初幾個循環的成長量可能不同於穩態。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Initial-cycle growth can differ from steady-state growth. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}},{"id":"a012-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-05"],"title":"熱式與電漿式","titleEn":"Compare thermal and plasma ALD","objective":"完成「熱式與電漿式」的工程驗收單，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for compare thermal and plasma ald, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱式與電漿式。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare thermal and plasma ALD. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「熱式與電漿式」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare thermal and plasma ald and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱式與電漿式」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for compare thermal and plasma ald: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-06-k1","title":"熱式與電漿式的原理","titleEn":"Compare thermal and plasma ALD principle","text":"活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。","textEn":"Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden."},{"id":"a012-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","textEn":"Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱式與電漿式」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare thermal and plasma ald?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden."],"answer":2,"explanation":"活性種來源不同，損傷與熱負荷也不同。 串聯介電層滿足電容倒數相加；若介面層電容較小，單純提高上層介電常數的整體收益有限。","explanationEn":"Different reactive-species sources change damage and thermal burden. Series capacitances add inversely; a small interfacial capacitance limits benefits from raising the upper-layer permittivity."}}]},{"id":"a012-stage02","order":2,"title":"表面循環","titleEn":"Surface cycles","description":"在「表面循環」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for surface cycles, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a012-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-06"],"title":"第一半反應","titleEn":"Trace the first half-reaction","objective":"完成「第一半反應」的因果圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace the first half-reaction, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：第一半反應。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace the first half-reaction. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「第一半反應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace the first half-reaction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「第一半反應」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace the first half-reaction: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-07-k1","title":"第一半反應的原理","titleEn":"Trace the first half-reaction principle","text":"飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。","textEn":"After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth."},{"id":"a012-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「第一半反應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace the first half-reaction?","options":["飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"飽和吸附後增加暴露不應無限增加單循環成長。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"After saturation, exposure should not indefinitely increase cycle growth. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-07"],"title":"清除殘留氣體","titleEn":"Separate purge from reaction","objective":"完成「清除殘留氣體」的對照表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for separate purge from reaction, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：清除殘留氣體。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate purge from reaction. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「清除殘留氣體」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate purge from reaction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「清除殘留氣體」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for separate purge from reaction: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-08-k1","title":"清除殘留氣體的原理","titleEn":"Separate purge from reaction principle","text":"不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。","textEn":"Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling."},{"id":"a012-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「清除殘留氣體」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate purge from reaction?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不足的清除會讓氣相反應混入表面循環。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"Insufficient purge allows gas-phase reactions into surface cycling. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-08"],"title":"第二半反應","titleEn":"Trace the second half-reaction","objective":"完成「第二半反應」的敏感度草圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for trace the second half-reaction, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：第二半反應。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace the second half-reaction. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「第二半反應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace the second half-reaction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「第二半反應」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for trace the second half-reaction: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-09-k1","title":"第二半反應的原理","titleEn":"Trace the second half-reaction principle","text":"共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。","textEn":"The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface."},{"id":"a012-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「第二半反應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace the second half-reaction?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共反應物需轉化已吸附物並建立下一循環表面。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"The co-reactant transforms adsorbates and prepares the next-cycle surface. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-09"],"title":"飽和曲線","titleEn":"Construct saturation curves","objective":"完成「飽和曲線」的故障判別表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for construct saturation curves, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：飽和曲線。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Construct saturation curves. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「飽和曲線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for construct saturation curves and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「飽和曲線」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for construct saturation curves: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-10-k1","title":"飽和曲線的原理","titleEn":"Construct saturation curves principle","text":"證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。","textEn":"Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point."},{"id":"a012-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「飽和曲線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating construct saturation curves?","options":["證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"證明飽和需要掃描暴露量而不是只看單一點。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"Saturation needs an exposure sweep rather than one operating point. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-10"],"title":"循環與膜厚","titleEn":"Relate cycles to thickness","objective":"完成「循環與膜厚」的量測規劃，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for relate cycles to thickness, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：循環與膜厚。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate cycles to thickness. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「循環與膜厚」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate cycles to thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「循環與膜厚」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for relate cycles to thickness: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-11-k1","title":"循環與膜厚的原理","titleEn":"Relate cycles to thickness principle","text":"線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。","textEn":"Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks."},{"id":"a012-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「循環與膜厚」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate cycles to thickness?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"線性外推需扣除成核截距並檢查成長模式。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"Linear extrapolation needs nucleation intercept and growth-mode checks. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}},{"id":"a012-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-11"],"title":"溫度窗","titleEn":"Identify the temperature window","objective":"完成「溫度窗」的工程驗收單，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for identify the temperature window, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度窗。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify the temperature window. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「溫度窗」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify the temperature window and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度窗」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for identify the temperature window: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-12-k1","title":"溫度窗的原理","titleEn":"Identify the temperature window principle","text":"太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。","textEn":"Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition."},{"id":"a012-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","textEn":"ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度窗」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify the temperature window?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"太低可能冷凝，太高可能熱分解。 ALD 的自限制反應需以暴露飽和證據確認；觀察到循環成長不等於已排除氣相 CVD 成分。","explanationEn":"Low temperature can cause condensation and high temperature decomposition. ALD self-limitation needs exposure-saturation evidence; cyclic growth alone does not rule out a gas-phase CVD contribution."}}]},{"id":"a012-stage03","order":3,"title":"三維覆蓋","titleEn":"Three-dimensional coverage","description":"在「三維覆蓋」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for three-dimensional coverage, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a012-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-12"],"title":"深槽反應物耗盡","titleEn":"Assess feature-scale depletion","objective":"完成「深槽反應物耗盡」的因果圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess feature-scale depletion, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：深槽反應物耗盡。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess feature-scale depletion. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「深槽反應物耗盡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess feature-scale depletion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「深槽反應物耗盡」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess feature-scale depletion: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-13-k1","title":"深槽反應物耗盡的原理","titleEn":"Assess feature-scale depletion principle","text":"入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。","textEn":"Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features."},{"id":"a012-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「深槽反應物耗盡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess feature-scale depletion?","options":["入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"入口飽和不代表高深寬比底部已飽和。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Entrance saturation does not prove bottom saturation in deep features. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-13"],"title":"側壁與底部比","titleEn":"Compare sidewall and bottom thickness","objective":"完成「側壁與底部比」的對照表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for compare sidewall and bottom thickness, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：側壁與底部比。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare sidewall and bottom thickness. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「側壁與底部比」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare sidewall and bottom thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「側壁與底部比」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for compare sidewall and bottom thickness: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-14-k1","title":"側壁與底部比的原理","titleEn":"Compare sidewall and bottom thickness principle","text":"覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。","textEn":"Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations."},{"id":"a012-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「側壁與底部比」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare sidewall and bottom thickness?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"覆蓋率須明確指定厚度比的兩個位置。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Conformality ratios need explicit measurement locations. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-14"],"title":"成分均勻性","titleEn":"Map composition uniformity","objective":"完成「成分均勻性」的敏感度草圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map composition uniformity, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：成分均勻性。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map composition uniformity. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「成分均勻性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map composition uniformity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「成分均勻性」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map composition uniformity: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-15-k1","title":"成分均勻性的原理","titleEn":"Map composition uniformity principle","text":"厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。","textEn":"Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition."},{"id":"a012-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「成分均勻性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map composition uniformity?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"厚度均勻不保證雜質與化學鍵分布均勻。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Uniform thickness does not guarantee uniform impurity or bonding composition. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-15"],"title":"針孔與漏電","titleEn":"Connect pinholes and leakage","objective":"完成「針孔與漏電」的故障判別表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for connect pinholes and leakage, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：針孔與漏電。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Connect pinholes and leakage. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「針孔與漏電」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for connect pinholes and leakage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「針孔與漏電」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for connect pinholes and leakage: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-16-k1","title":"針孔與漏電的原理","titleEn":"Connect pinholes and leakage principle","text":"少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。","textEn":"A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage."},{"id":"a012-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「針孔與漏電」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating connect pinholes and leakage?","options":["少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"少數局部缺陷可主導大面積漏電。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"A few local defects can dominate area-scale leakage. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-16"],"title":"晶化風險","titleEn":"Assess crystallization","objective":"完成「晶化風險」的量測規劃，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess crystallization, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶化風險。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess crystallization. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「晶化風險」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess crystallization and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶化風險」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess crystallization: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-17-k1","title":"晶化風險的原理","titleEn":"Assess crystallization principle","text":"後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。","textEn":"Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways."},{"id":"a012-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶化風險」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess crystallization?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"後續退火可能改變晶界與漏電路徑。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Later annealing can change grain boundaries and leakage pathways. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}},{"id":"a012-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-17"],"title":"殘碳分析","titleEn":"Interpret residual carbon","objective":"完成「殘碳分析」的工程驗收單，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for interpret residual carbon, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：殘碳分析。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret residual carbon. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「殘碳分析」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret residual carbon and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「殘碳分析」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for interpret residual carbon: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-18-k1","title":"殘碳分析的原理","titleEn":"Interpret residual carbon principle","text":"成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。","textEn":"Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata."},{"id":"a012-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","textEn":"Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「殘碳分析」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret residual carbon?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata."],"answer":2,"explanation":"成分量測深度與背景需跟殘留濃度一起報告。 狹窄特徵增加表面積與反應物消耗，入口暴露充分時，深處仍可能需要更長的傳輸時間。","explanationEn":"Residual concentration needs measurement-depth and background metadata. Narrow features increase surface area and reactant demand, so deep regions can require longer transport even with adequate entrance exposure."}}]},{"id":"a012-stage04","order":4,"title":"電性及整合","titleEn":"Electrical behavior and integration","description":"在「電性及整合」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for electrical behavior and integration, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a012-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-18"],"title":"介面偶極","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles","objective":"完成「介面偶極」的因果圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace interface dipoles, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：介面偶極。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace interface dipoles. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Interface chemistry can also change effective work function. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interface chemistry can also change effective work function. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「介面偶極」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace interface dipoles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「介面偶極」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace interface dipoles: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-19-k1","title":"介面偶極的原理","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles principle","text":"介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。","textEn":"Interface chemistry can also change effective work function."},{"id":"a012-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「介面偶極」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace interface dipoles?","options":["介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Interface chemistry can also change effective work function.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"介面化學可能同時改變有效功函數。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Interface chemistry can also change effective work function. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-19"],"title":"遷移率代價","titleEn":"Assess mobility tradeoffs","objective":"完成「遷移率代價」的對照表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess mobility tradeoffs, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：遷移率代價。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess mobility tradeoffs. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：閘極電容提高就足以證明載子遷移率提高，不必檢查散射或陷阱。 應回到「遷移率代價」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Higher gate capacitance alone proves higher carrier mobility without checking scattering or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess mobility tradeoffs and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「遷移率代價」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess mobility tradeoffs: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-20-k1","title":"遷移率代價的原理","titleEn":"Assess mobility tradeoffs principle","text":"高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。","textEn":"Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties."},{"id":"a012-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「遷移率代價」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess mobility tradeoffs?","options":["閘極電容提高就足以證明載子遷移率提高，不必檢查散射或陷阱。","高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。","兩種介電堆疊只要 EOT 相同，其介面散射與有效遷移率就必定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Higher gate capacitance alone proves higher carrier mobility without checking scattering or traps.","Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties.","Two dielectric stacks with equal EOT must have identical interface scattering and effective mobility."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高電容增益需與散射及陷阱造成的劣化比較。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Capacitance gain must be compared with scattering and trap penalties. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-20"],"title":"閘極填充空間","titleEn":"Budget gate-cavity volume","objective":"完成「閘極填充空間」的敏感度草圖，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for budget gate-cavity volume, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘極填充空間。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget gate-cavity volume. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「閘極填充空間」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget gate-cavity volume and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘極填充空間」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for budget gate-cavity volume: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-21-k1","title":"閘極填充空間的原理","titleEn":"Budget gate-cavity volume principle","text":"介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。","textEn":"Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume."},{"id":"a012-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘極填充空間」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget gate-cavity volume?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介電層變厚會消耗金屬可用填充空間。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Thicker dielectric consumes available metal-fill volume. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-21"],"title":"偏壓穩定性","titleEn":"Assess bias stability","objective":"完成「偏壓穩定性」的故障判別表，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess bias stability, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：偏壓穩定性。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess bias stability. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「偏壓穩定性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess bias stability and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「偏壓穩定性」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess bias stability: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-22-k1","title":"偏壓穩定性的原理","titleEn":"Assess bias stability principle","text":"初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。","textEn":"Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability."},{"id":"a012-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「偏壓穩定性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess bias stability?","options":["初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"初始良好電性不等於長時間偏壓穩定。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Good initial electrical behavior does not prove long-term bias stability. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-22"],"title":"配方變更見證","titleEn":"Define change-control witnesses","objective":"完成「配方變更見證」的量測規劃，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define change-control witnesses, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：配方變更見證。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define change-control witnesses. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「配方變更見證」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define change-control witnesses and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「配方變更見證」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define change-control witnesses: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-23-k1","title":"配方變更見證的原理","titleEn":"Define change-control witnesses principle","text":"換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。","textEn":"A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks."},{"id":"a012-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「配方變更見證」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define change-control witnesses?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"換前驅物要重新驗證覆蓋、雜質與可靠度。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"A precursor change requires renewed coverage, impurity and reliability checks. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}},{"id":"a012-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-ald","v8a-highk","v8a-oxide"],"prerequisiteIds":["a012-v8-23"],"title":"高介電層放行","titleEn":"Release the high-k layer","objective":"完成「高介電層放行」的工程驗收單，把EOT、飽和循環、三維覆蓋中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for release the high-k layer, connecting relevant limits in eot, saturated cycles and 3d coverage to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：高介電層放行。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Release the high-k layer. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「高介電層放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for release the high-k layer and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「高介電層放行」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for release the high-k layer: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a012-v8-24-k1","title":"高介電層放行的原理","titleEn":"Release the high-k layer principle","text":"EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。","textEn":"Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly."},{"id":"a012-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","textEn":"Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「高介電層放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating release the high-k layer?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"EOT、漏電、陷阱及三維覆蓋應共同審查。 低 EOT、低漏電及低陷阱密度是不同目標；改變介面處理可能改善其中一項卻犧牲另一項。","explanationEn":"Review EOT, leakage, traps and 3D coverage jointly. Low EOT, leakage and trap density are distinct objectives; an interface treatment may improve one while compromising another."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a013","title":"金屬閘極功函數工程","titleEn":"Metal-gate work-function engineering","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["能帶與閘極","材料堆疊","選擇性加工","閾值與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Band alignment and gates","Material stacks","Selective processing","Threshold and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a013-stage01","order":1,"title":"能帶與閘極","titleEn":"Band alignment and gates","description":"在「能帶與閘極」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for band alignment and gates, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"定義真空功函數","titleEn":"Define vacuum work function","objective":"完成「定義真空功函數」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for define vacuum work function, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：定義真空功函數。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define vacuum work function. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「定義真空功函數」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define vacuum work function and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「定義真空功函數」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for define vacuum work function: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-01-k1","title":"定義真空功函數的原理","titleEn":"Define vacuum work function principle","text":"金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。","textEn":"Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device."},{"id":"a013-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「定義真空功函數」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define vacuum work function?","options":["金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"金屬真空功函數不必等於器件中的有效功函數。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Vacuum work function need not equal effective work function in a device. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-01"],"title":"平帶條件","titleEn":"Draw flat-band conditions","objective":"完成「平帶條件」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for draw flat-band conditions, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：平帶條件。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw flat-band conditions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「平帶條件」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw flat-band conditions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「平帶條件」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for draw flat-band conditions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-02-k1","title":"平帶條件的原理","titleEn":"Draw flat-band conditions principle","text":"平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。","textEn":"Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge."},{"id":"a013-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「平帶條件」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw flat-band conditions?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平帶電壓也受介面電荷影響。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Flat-band voltage is also affected by interface charge. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-02"],"title":"NMOS 與 PMOS","titleEn":"Separate NMOS and PMOS targets","objective":"完成「NMOS 與 PMOS」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for separate nmos and pmos targets, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：NMOS 與 PMOS。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate NMOS and PMOS targets. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「NMOS 與 PMOS」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate nmos and pmos targets and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「NMOS 與 PMOS」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for separate nmos and pmos targets: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-03-k1","title":"NMOS 與 PMOS的原理","titleEn":"Separate NMOS and PMOS targets principle","text":"互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。","textEn":"Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies."},{"id":"a013-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「NMOS 與 PMOS」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate nmos and pmos targets?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"互補元件需要不同閾值設定策略。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Complementary devices need different threshold-setting strategies. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-03"],"title":"閘介電層串聯","titleEn":"Include the dielectric stack","objective":"完成「閘介電層串聯」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for include the dielectric stack, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘介電層串聯。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Include the dielectric stack. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閘介電層串聯」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for include the dielectric stack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘介電層串聯」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for include the dielectric stack: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-04-k1","title":"閘介電層串聯的原理","titleEn":"Include the dielectric stack principle","text":"相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。","textEn":"The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks."},{"id":"a013-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘介電層串聯」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating include the dielectric stack?","options":["相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。","沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks.","Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同金屬在不同介面堆疊可有不同有效功函數。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"The same metal can have different effective work functions in different stacks. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-04"],"title":"閾值抽取定義","titleEn":"Choose threshold extraction","objective":"完成「閾值抽取定義」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for choose threshold extraction, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閾值抽取定義。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose threshold extraction. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「閾值抽取定義」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose threshold extraction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閾值抽取定義」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for choose threshold extraction: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-05-k1","title":"閾值抽取定義的原理","titleEn":"Choose threshold extraction principle","text":"不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。","textEn":"Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds."},{"id":"a013-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閾值抽取定義」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose threshold extraction?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同抽取方法會產生不可直接混比的閾值。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Different extraction methods can yield noncomparable thresholds. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}},{"id":"a013-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-05"],"title":"厚度空間預算","titleEn":"Budget gate-stack thickness","objective":"完成「厚度空間預算」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for budget gate-stack thickness, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：厚度空間預算。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Budget gate-stack thickness. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。 應回到「厚度空間預算」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle. Revisit assumptions and sampling for budget gate-stack thickness and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「厚度空間預算」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for budget gate-stack thickness: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-06-k1","title":"厚度空間預算的原理","titleEn":"Budget gate-stack thickness principle","text":"奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。","textEn":"Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness."},{"id":"a013-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","textEn":"Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「厚度空間預算」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating budget gate-stack thickness?","options":["沉積循環數總能從第一循環精確線性外推。","厚度相同就代表介面電性相同。","奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness always extrapolates linearly from the first cycle.","Equal thickness implies equal interface electrical quality.","Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"奈米片間隙限制功函數金屬與填充金屬總厚度。 平帶及閾值由金屬、介電層、半導體與電荷共同決定，不能用單一金屬真空功函數直接替代整個堆疊。","explanationEn":"Nanosheet gaps limit total work-function and fill-metal thickness. Flat-band and threshold depend on metal, dielectric, semiconductor and charge; vacuum work function cannot replace the whole stack."}}]},{"id":"a013-stage02","order":2,"title":"材料堆疊","titleEn":"Material stacks","description":"在「材料堆疊」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for material stacks, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-06"],"title":"薄金屬連續性","titleEn":"Assess thin-metal continuity","objective":"完成「薄金屬連續性」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for assess thin-metal continuity, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：薄金屬連續性。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess thin-metal continuity. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「薄金屬連續性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess thin-metal continuity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「薄金屬連續性」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for assess thin-metal continuity: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-07-k1","title":"薄金屬連續性的原理","titleEn":"Assess thin-metal continuity principle","text":"極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。","textEn":"An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous."},{"id":"a013-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「薄金屬連續性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess thin-metal continuity?","options":["極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"極薄金屬可能未形成連續覆蓋。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"An ultrathin metal layer may not be continuous. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-07"],"title":"介面偶極形成","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles","objective":"完成「介面偶極形成」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for trace interface dipoles, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：介面偶極形成。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace interface dipoles. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Interface reactions can create additional band shifts. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Interface reactions can create additional band shifts. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「介面偶極形成」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace interface dipoles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「介面偶極形成」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for trace interface dipoles: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-08-k1","title":"介面偶極形成的原理","titleEn":"Trace interface dipoles principle","text":"介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。","textEn":"Interface reactions can create additional band shifts."},{"id":"a013-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「介面偶極形成」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace interface dipoles?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Interface reactions can create additional band shifts.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"介面反應可產生額外能帶位移。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Interface reactions can create additional band shifts. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-08"],"title":"氮含量與成分","titleEn":"Compare nitrogen and composition","objective":"完成「氮含量與成分」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare nitrogen and composition, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氮含量與成分。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare nitrogen and composition. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「氮含量與成分」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare nitrogen and composition and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氮含量與成分」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare nitrogen and composition: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-09-k1","title":"氮含量與成分的原理","titleEn":"Compare nitrogen and composition principle","text":"材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。","textEn":"A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function."},{"id":"a013-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氮含量與成分」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare nitrogen and composition?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料名稱相同不代表化學計量與功函數相同。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"A shared material name does not guarantee equal stoichiometry or work function. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-09"],"title":"晶粒與取向","titleEn":"Assess grain orientation","objective":"完成「晶粒與取向」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess grain orientation, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶粒與取向。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess grain orientation. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「晶粒與取向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess grain orientation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶粒與取向」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess grain orientation: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-10-k1","title":"晶粒與取向的原理","titleEn":"Assess grain orientation principle","text":"多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。","textEn":"Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences."},{"id":"a013-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶粒與取向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess grain orientation?","options":["多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。","入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences.","Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多晶金屬取向分布可帶來局部功函數差。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Polycrystalline orientation can introduce local work-function differences. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-10"],"title":"沉積成核","titleEn":"Inspect nucleation","objective":"完成「沉積成核」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inspect nucleation, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：沉積成核。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect nucleation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「沉積成核」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect nucleation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「沉積成核」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inspect nucleation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-11-k1","title":"沉積成核的原理","titleEn":"Inspect nucleation principle","text":"初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。","textEn":"Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior."},{"id":"a013-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「沉積成核」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect nucleation?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始成核差異會改變薄層完整性與界面。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Initial nucleation changes thin-layer integrity and interface behavior. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}},{"id":"a013-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-11"],"title":"熱處理重分布","titleEn":"Track thermal redistribution","objective":"完成「熱處理重分布」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for track thermal redistribution, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱處理重分布。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track thermal redistribution. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。 應回到「熱處理重分布」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track thermal redistribution and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱處理重分布」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for track thermal redistribution: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-12-k1","title":"熱處理重分布的原理","titleEn":"Track thermal redistribution principle","text":"元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。","textEn":"Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack."},{"id":"a013-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","textEn":"Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱處理重分布」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track thermal redistribution?","options":["入口飽和就證明深槽底部已飽和。","平均成分足以排除局部相分離。","元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。"],"optionsEn":["Entrance saturation proves deep-feature bottom saturation.","Mean composition rules out local phase separation.","Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack."],"answer":2,"explanation":"元素擴散會改變原先設計的閘堆疊。 超薄功函數層可能受成核、晶粒及介面反應影響；材料化學式相同不代表局部有效功函數相同。","explanationEn":"Element diffusion can alter the intended gate stack. Ultrathin work-function layers depend on nucleation, grains and reactions; equal formulas do not ensure equal local effective work function."}}]},{"id":"a013-stage03","order":3,"title":"選擇性加工","titleEn":"Selective processing","description":"在「選擇性加工」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for selective processing, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-12"],"title":"區域保護層","titleEn":"Plan regional protection","objective":"完成「區域保護層」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for plan regional protection, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：區域保護層。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Plan regional protection. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「區域保護層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for plan regional protection and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「區域保護層」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for plan regional protection: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-13-k1","title":"區域保護層的原理","titleEn":"Plan regional protection principle","text":"選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。","textEn":"Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack."},{"id":"a013-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「區域保護層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating plan regional protection?","options":["選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"選擇處理一種元件時需保護另一種閘堆疊。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Processing one device polarity requires protecting the other stack. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-13"],"title":"金屬回蝕","titleEn":"Assess metal recess","objective":"完成「金屬回蝕」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess metal recess, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬回蝕。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess metal recess. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「金屬回蝕」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess metal recess and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬回蝕」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess metal recess: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-14-k1","title":"金屬回蝕的原理","titleEn":"Assess metal recess principle","text":"回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。","textEn":"Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage."},{"id":"a013-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬回蝕」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess metal recess?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"回蝕深度誤差可能破壞有效功函數層覆蓋。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Recess errors can compromise work-function-layer coverage. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-14"],"title":"選擇性去除","titleEn":"Check selective removal","objective":"完成「選擇性去除」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for check selective removal, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：選擇性去除。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check selective removal. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「選擇性去除」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check selective removal and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「選擇性去除」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for check selective removal: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-15-k1","title":"選擇性去除的原理","titleEn":"Check selective removal principle","text":"去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。","textEn":"Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement."},{"id":"a013-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「選擇性去除」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check selective removal?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"去除上層金屬仍須量化下層損失。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Removing an upper metal still requires lower-layer loss measurement. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-15"],"title":"窄腔填充","titleEn":"Inspect narrow-cavity fill","objective":"完成「窄腔填充」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect narrow-cavity fill, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：窄腔填充。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect narrow-cavity fill. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Premature closure can conceal internal voids. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Premature closure can conceal internal voids. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「窄腔填充」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect narrow-cavity fill and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「窄腔填充」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect narrow-cavity fill: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-16-k1","title":"窄腔填充的原理","titleEn":"Inspect narrow-cavity fill principle","text":"外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。","textEn":"Premature closure can conceal internal voids."},{"id":"a013-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「窄腔填充」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect narrow-cavity fill?","options":["外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。","高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["Premature closure can conceal internal voids.","High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外部封口可能掩蓋內部空洞。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Premature closure can conceal internal voids. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-16"],"title":"閘極電阻","titleEn":"Separate gate resistance","objective":"完成「閘極電阻」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for separate gate resistance, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閘極電阻。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate gate resistance. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「閘極電阻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate gate resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閘極電阻」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for separate gate resistance: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-17-k1","title":"閘極電阻的原理","titleEn":"Separate gate resistance principle","text":"低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。","textEn":"Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria."},{"id":"a013-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閘極電阻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate gate resistance?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低閘電阻與正確閾值是不同驗收項目。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Low gate resistance and correct threshold are separate criteria. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}},{"id":"a013-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-17"],"title":"金屬殘留短路","titleEn":"Locate residual-metal bridges","objective":"完成「金屬殘留短路」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for locate residual-metal bridges, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬殘留短路。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 做一張閾值歸因表：列金屬功函數、介面電荷及通道摻雜三個可能原因；為各原因分別指定材料分析、C-V 或摻雜輪廓的辨別證據。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Locate residual-metal bridges. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Build a threshold-attribution table for metal work function, interface charge and channel doping. Assign discriminating materials, C-V or doping-profile evidence to each.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。 應回到「金屬殘留短路」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps. Revisit assumptions and sampling for locate residual-metal bridges and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬殘留短路」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for locate residual-metal bridges: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-18-k1","title":"金屬殘留短路的原理","titleEn":"Locate residual-metal bridges principle","text":"局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。","textEn":"Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates."},{"id":"a013-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","textEn":"A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬殘留短路」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating locate residual-metal bridges?","options":["高介電常數保證沒有漏電及陷阱。","去除上層材料不需檢查下層損失。","局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。"],"optionsEn":["High permittivity guarantees no leakage or traps.","Removing an upper layer needs no lower-layer loss check.","Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部殘留可能在電性上連接原本隔離的閘。 狹窄閘腔的厚度總和受幾何約束，增加一層材料會減少其他層可用空間並可能形成空洞。","explanationEn":"Local residues can electrically connect isolated gates. A narrow gate cavity limits total stack thickness; adding one layer reduces space for others and can promote voids."}}]},{"id":"a013-stage04","order":4,"title":"閾值與可靠度","titleEn":"Threshold and reliability","description":"在「閾值與可靠度」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for threshold and reliability, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a013-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-18"],"title":"C-V 與 I-V","titleEn":"Cross-check C-V and I-V","objective":"完成「C-V 與 I-V」的因果圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for cross-check c-v and i-v, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：C-V 與 I-V。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Cross-check C-V and I-V. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「C-V 與 I-V」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for cross-check c-v and i-v and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「C-V 與 I-V」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for cross-check c-v and i-v: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-19-k1","title":"C-V 與 I-V的原理","titleEn":"Cross-check C-V and I-V principle","text":"兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。","textEn":"C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities."},{"id":"a013-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「C-V 與 I-V」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating cross-check c-v and i-v?","options":["兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩種量測對介面與通道的敏感度不同。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"C-V and I-V have different interface and channel sensitivities. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-19"],"title":"閾值空間圖","titleEn":"Map threshold variation","objective":"完成「閾值空間圖」的對照表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for map threshold variation, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：閾值空間圖。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map threshold variation. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「閾值空間圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map threshold variation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「閾值空間圖」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for map threshold variation: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-20-k1","title":"閾值空間圖的原理","titleEn":"Map threshold variation principle","text":"均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。","textEn":"An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures."},{"id":"a013-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「閾值空間圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map threshold variation?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"均值合格仍可能有尾端分布問題。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"An acceptable mean can coexist with distribution-tail failures. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-20"],"title":"溫度依賴","titleEn":"Compare temperature dependence","objective":"完成「溫度依賴」的敏感度草圖，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for compare temperature dependence, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度依賴。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare temperature dependence. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「溫度依賴」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare temperature dependence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度依賴」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for compare temperature dependence: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-21-k1","title":"溫度依賴的原理","titleEn":"Compare temperature dependence principle","text":"不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。","textEn":"Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions."},{"id":"a013-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度依賴」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare temperature dependence?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同溫度的閾值不能忽略量測條件直接比較。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"Threshold comparisons across temperatures need matched measurement definitions. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-21"],"title":"偏壓老化","titleEn":"Track bias aging","objective":"完成「偏壓老化」的故障判別表，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for track bias aging, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：偏壓老化。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track bias aging. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「偏壓老化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track bias aging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「偏壓老化」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for track bias aging: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-22-k1","title":"偏壓老化的原理","titleEn":"Track bias aging principle","text":"閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。","textEn":"Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets."},{"id":"a013-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「偏壓老化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track bias aging?","options":["閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。","低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets.","Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"閾值漂移需要與初始製程偏移分開。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"Aging drift must be separated from initial process offsets. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-22"],"title":"雙極性整合","titleEn":"Review dual-polarity integration","objective":"完成「雙極性整合」的量測規劃，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for review dual-polarity integration, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：雙極性整合。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review dual-polarity integration. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「雙極性整合」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review dual-polarity integration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「雙極性整合」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for review dual-polarity integration: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-23-k1","title":"雙極性整合的原理","titleEn":"Review dual-polarity integration principle","text":"NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。","textEn":"NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation."},{"id":"a013-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「雙極性整合」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review dual-polarity integration?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"NMOS 改善不應以未檢查的 PMOS 退化交換。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"NMOS improvement must not hide untested PMOS degradation. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}},{"id":"a013-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-highk","v8a-ald","v8a-scaling"],"prerequisiteIds":["a013-v8-23"],"title":"金屬閘極驗收","titleEn":"Accept the metal gate","objective":"完成「金屬閘極驗收」的工程驗收單，把有效功函數、閾值分布、閘填充中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept the metal gate, connecting relevant limits in effective work function, threshold distribution and gate fill to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：金屬閘極驗收。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept the metal gate. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。 應回到「金屬閘極驗收」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept the metal gate and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「金屬閘極驗收」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept the metal gate: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a013-v8-24-k1","title":"金屬閘極驗收的原理","titleEn":"Accept the metal gate principle","text":"功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。","textEn":"Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging."},{"id":"a013-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","textEn":"Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「金屬閘極驗收」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept the metal gate?","options":["低塊材電阻率保證低界面接觸電阻。","較快成長永遠改善圖案選擇性。","功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。"],"optionsEn":["Low bulk resistivity guarantees low interface contact resistance.","Faster growth always improves pattern selectivity.","Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging."],"answer":2,"explanation":"功函數、覆蓋、電阻、分布及老化需聯合判讀。 製程造成的初始閾值偏移與偏壓老化漂移需分開記錄，才能判斷改良來自材料設定還是可靠度變化。","explanationEn":"Jointly assess work function, coverage, resistance, distributions and aging. Separate initial process-induced threshold shifts from bias-aging drift to distinguish material tuning from reliability changes."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a014","title":"離子佈植摻雜","titleEn":"Ion implantation doping","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解劑量、射程、損傷及活化，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore dose, range, damage and activation through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["佈植目的與輪廓","束流與遮罩","損傷與活化","量測及整合"],"labelsEn":["Implant purpose and profiles","Beam and masks","Damage and activation","Measurement and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a014-stage01","order":1,"title":"佈植目的與輪廓","titleEn":"Implant purpose and profiles","description":"在「佈植目的與輪廓」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for implant purpose and profiles, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a014-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"劑量與濃度","titleEn":"Separate dose and concentration","objective":"完成「劑量與濃度」的因果圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate dose and concentration, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：劑量與濃度。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂積分題：假設一段厚 10 nm 的均勻區濃度為 10^19 cm^-3；先把厚度換成 cm，再求面劑量，並解釋此方盒輪廓不是實際佈植高斯輪廓。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate dose and concentration. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical integral: a uniform 10 nm region has concentration 10^19 cm^-3. Convert thickness to cm and compute areal dose; explain why this box profile is not a real implantation Gaussian.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「劑量與濃度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate dose and concentration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「劑量與濃度」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate dose and concentration: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-01-k1","title":"劑量與濃度的原理","titleEn":"Separate dose and concentration principle","text":"面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。","textEn":"Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings."},{"id":"a014-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「劑量與濃度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate dose and concentration?","options":["面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"面劑量與體濃度的單位及物理意義不同。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Areal dose and volume concentration have different units and meanings. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-01"],"title":"摻雜種類","titleEn":"Choose dopant roles","objective":"完成「摻雜種類」的對照表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for choose dopant roles, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：摻雜種類。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Choose dopant roles. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「摻雜種類」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for choose dopant roles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「摻雜種類」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for choose dopant roles: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-02-k1","title":"摻雜種類的原理","titleEn":"Choose dopant roles principle","text":"摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。","textEn":"Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior."},{"id":"a014-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「摻雜種類」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating choose dopant roles?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"摻雜元素與晶格佔位共同決定電性作用。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Dopant species and lattice occupation jointly determine electrical behavior. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-02"],"title":"投影射程","titleEn":"Read projected range","objective":"完成「投影射程」的敏感度草圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for read projected range, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：投影射程。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read projected range. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「投影射程」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read projected range and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「投影射程」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for read projected range: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-03-k1","title":"投影射程的原理","titleEn":"Read projected range principle","text":"射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。","textEn":"Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail."},{"id":"a014-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「投影射程」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read projected range?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail."],"answer":2,"explanation":"射程平均值不能代表整個深度分布尾端。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Mean projected range does not represent the depth-distribution tail. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-03"],"title":"能量與深度","titleEn":"Relate energy and depth","objective":"完成「能量與深度」的故障判別表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for relate energy and depth, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：能量與深度。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate energy and depth. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Energy affects both depth and damage distribution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Energy affects both depth and damage distribution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「能量與深度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate energy and depth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「能量與深度」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for relate energy and depth: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-04-k1","title":"能量與深度的原理","titleEn":"Relate energy and depth principle","text":"能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。","textEn":"Energy affects both depth and damage distribution."},{"id":"a014-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「能量與深度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate energy and depth?","options":["能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Energy affects both depth and damage distribution.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"能量影響深度，也同時影響損傷分布。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Energy affects both depth and damage distribution. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-04"],"title":"接面位置","titleEn":"Define junction depth","objective":"完成「接面位置」的量測規劃，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for define junction depth, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接面位置。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define junction depth. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「接面位置」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define junction depth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接面位置」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for define junction depth: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-05-k1","title":"接面位置的原理","titleEn":"Define junction depth principle","text":"接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。","textEn":"Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping."},{"id":"a014-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接面位置」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define junction depth?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接面需由摻雜輪廓與背景濃度交會判斷。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Junction depth depends on profile intersection with background doping. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}},{"id":"a014-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-05"],"title":"遮罩止擋條件","titleEn":"Set mask-stopping evidence","objective":"完成「遮罩止擋條件」的工程驗收單，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for set mask-stopping evidence, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：遮罩止擋條件。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Set mask-stopping evidence. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「遮罩止擋條件」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for set mask-stopping evidence and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「遮罩止擋條件」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for set mask-stopping evidence: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-06-k1","title":"遮罩止擋條件的原理","titleEn":"Set mask-stopping evidence principle","text":"遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。","textEn":"Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions."},{"id":"a014-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","textEn":"Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「遮罩止擋條件」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating set mask-stopping evidence?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"遮罩厚度須考慮射程展寬與薄弱區。 面劑量是深度濃度的積分；相同劑量可透過不同射程展寬形成不同峰值濃度。","explanationEn":"Mask thickness must account for range spread and weak regions. Areal dose is the depth integral of concentration; equal doses can have different peaks because of range spread."}}]},{"id":"a014-stage02","order":2,"title":"束流與遮罩","titleEn":"Beam and masks","description":"在「束流與遮罩」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for beam and masks, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a014-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-06"],"title":"質量分析","titleEn":"Trace mass selection","objective":"完成「質量分析」的因果圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trace mass selection, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：質量分析。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace mass selection. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「質量分析」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace mass selection and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「質量分析」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trace mass selection: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-07-k1","title":"質量分析的原理","titleEn":"Trace mass selection principle","text":"電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。","textEn":"Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species."},{"id":"a014-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「質量分析」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace mass selection?","options":["電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電荷質量比選擇有助區分束流物種。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Mass-to-charge selection helps distinguish beam species. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-07"],"title":"束流積分","titleEn":"Integrate beam dose","objective":"完成「束流積分」的對照表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for integrate beam dose, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：束流積分。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Integrate beam dose. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「束流積分」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for integrate beam dose and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「束流積分」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for integrate beam dose: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-08-k1","title":"束流積分的原理","titleEn":"Integrate beam dose principle","text":"電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。","textEn":"Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area."},{"id":"a014-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「束流積分」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating integrate beam dose?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"電流積分轉成劑量需要電荷態與照射面積。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Converting integrated current to dose requires charge state and area. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-08"],"title":"掃描均勻性","titleEn":"Assess scan uniformity","objective":"完成「掃描均勻性」的敏感度草圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess scan uniformity, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：掃描均勻性。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess scan uniformity. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「掃描均勻性」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess scan uniformity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「掃描均勻性」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess scan uniformity: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-09-k1","title":"掃描均勻性的原理","titleEn":"Assess scan uniformity principle","text":"掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。","textEn":"Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose."},{"id":"a014-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「掃描均勻性」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess scan uniformity?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose."],"answer":2,"explanation":"掃描速度與束流分布共同決定面劑量。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Scan speed and beam profile jointly determine areal dose. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-09"],"title":"晶向通道效應","titleEn":"Assess channeling","objective":"完成「晶向通道效應」的故障判別表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for assess channeling, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶向通道效應。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess channeling. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「晶向通道效應」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess channeling and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶向通道效應」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for assess channeling: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-10-k1","title":"晶向通道效應的原理","titleEn":"Assess channeling principle","text":"沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。","textEn":"Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails."},{"id":"a014-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶向通道效應」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess channeling?","options":["沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿晶體通道的離子可能產生較深尾端。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Ions aligned with crystal channels can create deeper tails. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-10"],"title":"傾角與陰影","titleEn":"Assess tilt and shadowing","objective":"完成「傾角與陰影」的量測規劃，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess tilt and shadowing, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：傾角與陰影。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess tilt and shadowing. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「傾角與陰影」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess tilt and shadowing and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「傾角與陰影」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess tilt and shadowing: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-11-k1","title":"傾角與陰影的原理","titleEn":"Assess tilt and shadowing principle","text":"抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。","textEn":"Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing."},{"id":"a014-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「傾角與陰影」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess tilt and shadowing?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"抑制通道效應的角度也可能增加圖案遮蔽。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Angles suppressing channeling can increase pattern shadowing. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}},{"id":"a014-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-11"],"title":"晶圓充電","titleEn":"Assess wafer charging","objective":"完成「晶圓充電」的工程驗收單，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess wafer charging, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：晶圓充電。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess wafer charging. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「晶圓充電」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess wafer charging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「晶圓充電」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess wafer charging: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-12-k1","title":"晶圓充電的原理","titleEn":"Assess wafer charging principle","text":"絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。","textEn":"Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage."},{"id":"a014-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","textEn":"Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「晶圓充電」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess wafer charging?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"絕緣結構上的電荷累積可能造成損傷。 晶體通道效應與圖案遮蔽是不同方向性問題；改變佈植角度時需同時檢查兩者。","explanationEn":"Charge accumulation on insulating structures can cause damage. Crystal channeling and pattern shadowing are different directional problems; changing implant angle requires evaluating both."}}]},{"id":"a014-stage03","order":3,"title":"損傷與活化","titleEn":"Damage and activation","description":"在「損傷與活化」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for damage and activation, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a014-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-12"],"title":"碰撞損傷","titleEn":"Map collision damage","objective":"完成「碰撞損傷」的因果圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for map collision damage, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：碰撞損傷。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map collision damage. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「碰撞損傷」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map collision damage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「碰撞損傷」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for map collision damage: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-13-k1","title":"碰撞損傷的原理","titleEn":"Map collision damage principle","text":"佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。","textEn":"Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration."},{"id":"a014-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「碰撞損傷」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map collision damage?","options":["佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"佈植後的化學濃度不代表可用載子濃度。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"Post-implant chemical concentration is not active carrier concentration. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-13"],"title":"非晶化區","titleEn":"Identify amorphized regions","objective":"完成「非晶化區」的對照表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for identify amorphized regions, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：非晶化區。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify amorphized regions. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「非晶化區」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify amorphized regions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「非晶化區」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for identify amorphized regions: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-14-k1","title":"非晶化區的原理","titleEn":"Identify amorphized regions principle","text":"非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。","textEn":"Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing."},{"id":"a014-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「非晶化區」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify amorphized regions?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"非晶層與晶體的退火恢復機制不同。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"Amorphous and crystalline regions recover differently during annealing. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-14"],"title":"暫態增強擴散","titleEn":"Identify transient enhanced diffusion","objective":"完成「暫態增強擴散」的敏感度草圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for identify transient enhanced diffusion, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：暫態增強擴散。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify transient enhanced diffusion. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「暫態增強擴散」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify transient enhanced diffusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「暫態增強擴散」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for identify transient enhanced diffusion: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-15-k1","title":"暫態增強擴散的原理","titleEn":"Identify transient enhanced diffusion principle","text":"過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。","textEn":"Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion."},{"id":"a014-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「暫態增強擴散」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify transient enhanced diffusion?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"過量點缺陷可在退火初期增強摻雜擴散。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"Excess point defects can enhance early anneal diffusion. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-15"],"title":"活化比例","titleEn":"Estimate activation fraction","objective":"完成「活化比例」的故障判別表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for estimate activation fraction, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：活化比例。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate activation fraction. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「活化比例」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate activation fraction and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「活化比例」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for estimate activation fraction: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-16-k1","title":"活化比例的原理","titleEn":"Estimate activation fraction principle","text":"活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。","textEn":"Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence."},{"id":"a014-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「活化比例」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate activation fraction?","options":["活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"活化比例需化學與電性濃度的配對證據。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"Activation needs paired chemical and electrical concentration evidence. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-16"],"title":"聚集與失活","titleEn":"Assess clustering and deactivation","objective":"完成「聚集與失活」的量測規劃，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess clustering and deactivation, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：聚集與失活。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess clustering and deactivation. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「聚集與失活」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess clustering and deactivation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「聚集與失活」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess clustering and deactivation: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-17-k1","title":"聚集與失活的原理","titleEn":"Assess clustering and deactivation principle","text":"更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。","textEn":"More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers."},{"id":"a014-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「聚集與失活」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess clustering and deactivation?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"更多摻雜原子未必產生等比例自由載子。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"More dopant atoms need not produce proportional free carriers. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}},{"id":"a014-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-17"],"title":"遮罩去除風險","titleEn":"Review mask stripping","objective":"完成「遮罩去除風險」的工程驗收單，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review mask stripping, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：遮罩去除風險。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review mask stripping. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「遮罩去除風險」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review mask stripping and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「遮罩去除風險」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review mask stripping: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-18-k1","title":"遮罩去除風險的原理","titleEn":"Review mask stripping principle","text":"高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。","textEn":"High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty."},{"id":"a014-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","textEn":"Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「遮罩去除風險」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review mask stripping?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高劑量佈植可能改變光阻移除難度。 佈植造成的空位及間隙原子會在退火中演化，活化與暫態擴散不能只由初始化學濃度預測。","explanationEn":"High-dose implantation can change resist-removal difficulty. Implant vacancies and interstitials evolve during annealing; activation and transient diffusion cannot follow from initial chemical concentration alone."}}]},{"id":"a014-stage04","order":4,"title":"量測及整合","titleEn":"Measurement and integration","description":"在「量測及整合」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for measurement and integration, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a014-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-18"],"title":"SIMS 深度校準","titleEn":"Calibrate SIMS depth","objective":"完成「SIMS 深度校準」的因果圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for calibrate sims depth, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：SIMS 深度校準。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Calibrate SIMS depth. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「SIMS 深度校準」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for calibrate sims depth and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「SIMS 深度校準」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for calibrate sims depth: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-19-k1","title":"SIMS 深度校準的原理","titleEn":"Calibrate SIMS depth principle","text":"濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。","textEn":"Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration."},{"id":"a014-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「SIMS 深度校準」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating calibrate sims depth?","options":["濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濺鍍時間轉深度需材料相關校準。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Converting sputter time to depth needs material-dependent calibration. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-19"],"title":"片電阻判讀","titleEn":"Interpret sheet resistance","objective":"完成「片電阻判讀」的對照表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for interpret sheet resistance, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片電阻判讀。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Interpret sheet resistance. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「片電阻判讀」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for interpret sheet resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片電阻判讀」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for interpret sheet resistance: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-20-k1","title":"片電阻判讀的原理","titleEn":"Interpret sheet resistance principle","text":"片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。","textEn":"Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth."},{"id":"a014-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片電阻判讀」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating interpret sheet resistance?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"片電阻綜合濃度、遷移率與活化層厚度。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Sheet resistance integrates concentration, mobility and active-layer depth. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-20"],"title":"接面漏電","titleEn":"Inspect junction leakage","objective":"完成「接面漏電」的敏感度草圖，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for inspect junction leakage, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接面漏電。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect junction leakage. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「接面漏電」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect junction leakage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接面漏電」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for inspect junction leakage: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-21-k1","title":"接面漏電的原理","titleEn":"Inspect junction leakage principle","text":"低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。","textEn":"Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal."},{"id":"a014-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接面漏電」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect junction leakage?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"低片電阻不保證接面損傷已消除。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Low sheet resistance does not prove junction damage removal. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-21"],"title":"多重能量設計","titleEn":"Compare multi-energy profiles","objective":"完成「多重能量設計」的故障判別表，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare multi-energy profiles, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：多重能量設計。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare multi-energy profiles. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「多重能量設計」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare multi-energy profiles and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「多重能量設計」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare multi-energy profiles: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-22-k1","title":"多重能量設計的原理","titleEn":"Compare multi-energy profiles principle","text":"多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。","textEn":"Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate."},{"id":"a014-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「多重能量設計」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare multi-energy profiles?","options":["多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多次佈植的輪廓需先在同一深度座標相加。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Multiple implant profiles must be summed on a shared depth coordinate. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-22"],"title":"熱歷程追蹤","titleEn":"Track subsequent heat treatments","objective":"完成「熱歷程追蹤」的量測規劃，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for track subsequent heat treatments, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱歷程追蹤。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track subsequent heat treatments. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「熱歷程追蹤」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track subsequent heat treatments and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱歷程追蹤」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for track subsequent heat treatments: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-23-k1","title":"熱歷程追蹤的原理","titleEn":"Track subsequent heat treatments principle","text":"佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。","textEn":"Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing."},{"id":"a014-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱歷程追蹤」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track subsequent heat treatments?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"佈植驗收需考慮後續製程的再次擴散。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Implant acceptance must consider diffusion during later processing. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}},{"id":"a014-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-implant","v8a-implantmask","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a014-v8-23"],"title":"佈植批次審查","titleEn":"Review the implant lot","objective":"完成「佈植批次審查」的工程驗收單，把劑量、射程、損傷及活化中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for review the implant lot, connecting relevant limits in dose, range, damage and activation to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：佈植批次審查。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Review the implant lot. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「佈植批次審查」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for review the implant lot and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「佈植批次審查」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for review the implant lot: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a014-v8-24-k1","title":"佈植批次審查的原理","titleEn":"Review the implant lot principle","text":"劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。","textEn":"Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together."},{"id":"a014-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","textEn":"SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「佈植批次審查」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating review the implant lot?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"劑量、深度、均勻、損傷及活化缺一不可。 SIMS 提供化學輪廓，電性量測反映活化載子與遷移率；兩種資料的深度及面積需一致才能比較。","explanationEn":"Review dose, depth, uniformity, damage and activation together. SIMS gives chemical profiles while electrical measurements reflect active carriers and mobility; align depth and area before comparing."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a015","title":"快速熱退火","titleEn":"Rapid thermal annealing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["退火需求","升降溫控制","電性與形貌","製程窗口"],"labelsEn":["Annealing requirements","Heating and cooling","Electrical and structural outcomes","Process-window evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a015-stage01","order":1,"title":"退火需求","titleEn":"Annealing requirements","description":"在「退火需求」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for annealing requirements, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a015-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"活化與擴散","titleEn":"Separate activation and diffusion","objective":"完成「活化與擴散」的因果圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate activation and diffusion, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：活化與擴散。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate activation and diffusion. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「活化與擴散」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate activation and diffusion and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「活化與擴散」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate activation and diffusion: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-01-k1","title":"活化與擴散的原理","titleEn":"Separate activation and diffusion principle","text":"活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。","textEn":"Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution."},{"id":"a015-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「活化與擴散」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate activation and diffusion?","options":["活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"活化提高載子可用性，擴散改變空間分布。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Activation changes carrier availability while diffusion changes spatial distribution. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-01"],"title":"溫度時間軌跡","titleEn":"Draw temperature-time trajectories","objective":"完成「溫度時間軌跡」的對照表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for draw temperature-time trajectories, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度時間軌跡。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Draw temperature-time trajectories. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「溫度時間軌跡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for draw temperature-time trajectories and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度時間軌跡」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for draw temperature-time trajectories: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-02-k1","title":"溫度時間軌跡的原理","titleEn":"Draw temperature-time trajectories principle","text":"峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。","textEn":"Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure."},{"id":"a015-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度時間軌跡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating draw temperature-time trajectories?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"峰值溫度相同不代表總熱暴露相同。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Equal peak temperature does not imply equal thermal exposure. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-02"],"title":"熱預算積分","titleEn":"Construct a thermal-budget integral","objective":"完成「熱預算積分」的敏感度草圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for construct a thermal-budget integral, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱預算積分。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂兩段熱歷程：用任意擴散係數 D1=1、D2=4 與時間 t1=4、t2=1 比較 D×t；說明同一擴散積分仍不證明活化或缺陷演化相同。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Construct a thermal-budget integral. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical thermal histories: compare D×t for arbitrary diffusivities D1=1, D2=4 and times t1=4, t2=1. Explain why equal integrated diffusion does not prove equal activation or defect evolution.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「熱預算積分」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for construct a thermal-budget integral and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱預算積分」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for construct a thermal-budget integral: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-03-k1","title":"熱預算積分的原理","titleEn":"Construct a thermal-budget integral principle","text":"擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。","textEn":"Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone."},{"id":"a015-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱預算積分」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating construct a thermal-budget integral?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"擴散預算應考慮溫度依賴係數而非只加時間。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Diffusion budgets need temperature-dependent coefficients, not time alone. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-03"],"title":"損傷恢復","titleEn":"Define damage-recovery targets","objective":"完成「損傷恢復」的故障判別表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for define damage-recovery targets, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：損傷恢復。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Define damage-recovery targets. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「損傷恢復」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for define damage-recovery targets and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「損傷恢復」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for define damage-recovery targets: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-04-k1","title":"損傷恢復的原理","titleEn":"Define damage-recovery targets principle","text":"缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。","textEn":"Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales."},{"id":"a015-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「損傷恢復」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating define damage-recovery targets?","options":["缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺陷修復與摻雜活化可有不同時間尺度。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Damage repair and dopant activation can have different timescales. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-04"],"title":"前段堆疊","titleEn":"Inventory the incoming stack","objective":"完成「前段堆疊」的量測規劃，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for inventory the incoming stack, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：前段堆疊。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inventory the incoming stack. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「前段堆疊」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inventory the incoming stack and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「前段堆疊」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for inventory the incoming stack: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-05-k1","title":"前段堆疊的原理","titleEn":"Inventory the incoming stack principle","text":"表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。","textEn":"Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer."},{"id":"a015-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「前段堆疊」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inventory the incoming stack?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面材料會改變吸收、發射與熱傳。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Surface materials change absorption, emission and heat transfer. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}},{"id":"a015-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-05"],"title":"氣氛角色","titleEn":"Assign ambient functions","objective":"完成「氣氛角色」的工程驗收單，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assign ambient functions, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：氣氛角色。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assign ambient functions. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「氣氛角色」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assign ambient functions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「氣氛角色」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assign ambient functions: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-06-k1","title":"氣氛角色的原理","titleEn":"Assign ambient functions principle","text":"氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。","textEn":"Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport."},{"id":"a015-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","textEn":"Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「氣氛角色」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assign ambient functions?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport."],"answer":2,"explanation":"氣氛可影響氧化與界面，不只是傳熱背景。 擴散長度與時間積分的擴散係數相關，因此短而熱與長而冷的處理不能只用最高溫度排序。","explanationEn":"Ambient affects oxidation and interfaces beyond thermal transport. Diffusion length relates to integrated diffusivity, so short-hot and long-cool cycles cannot be ranked by peak temperature alone."}}]},{"id":"a015-stage02","order":2,"title":"升降溫控制","titleEn":"Heating and cooling","description":"在「升降溫控制」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for heating and cooling, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a015-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-06"],"title":"燈區分配","titleEn":"Allocate heating zones","objective":"完成「燈區分配」的因果圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for allocate heating zones, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：燈區分配。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Allocate heating zones. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「燈區分配」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for allocate heating zones and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「燈區分配」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for allocate heating zones: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-07-k1","title":"燈區分配的原理","titleEn":"Allocate heating zones principle","text":"多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。","textEn":"Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling."},{"id":"a015-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「燈區分配」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating allocate heating zones?","options":["多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多區加熱需要處理區域之間的熱耦合。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Multizone heating must account for thermal coupling. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-07"],"title":"高溫計發射率","titleEn":"Assess pyrometer emissivity","objective":"完成「高溫計發射率」的對照表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess pyrometer emissivity, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：高溫計發射率。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess pyrometer emissivity. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「高溫計發射率」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess pyrometer emissivity and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「高溫計發射率」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess pyrometer emissivity: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-08-k1","title":"高溫計發射率的原理","titleEn":"Assess pyrometer emissivity principle","text":"亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。","textEn":"Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model."},{"id":"a015-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「高溫計發射率」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess pyrometer emissivity?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"亮度溫度取決於材料發射率模型。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Brightness temperature depends on the emissivity model. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-08"],"title":"背面狀態","titleEn":"Check backside conditions","objective":"完成「背面狀態」的敏感度草圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for check backside conditions, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：背面狀態。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Check backside conditions. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「背面狀態」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for check backside conditions and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「背面狀態」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for check backside conditions: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-09-k1","title":"背面狀態的原理","titleEn":"Check backside conditions principle","text":"背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。","textEn":"Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings."},{"id":"a015-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「背面狀態」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating check backside conditions?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"背面薄膜與粗糙度可能改變溫度讀值。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Backside films and roughness can alter temperature readings. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-09"],"title":"升溫斜率","titleEn":"Compare ramp rates","objective":"完成「升溫斜率」的故障判別表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for compare ramp rates, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：升溫斜率。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare ramp rates. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「升溫斜率」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare ramp rates and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「升溫斜率」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for compare ramp rates: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-10-k1","title":"升溫斜率的原理","titleEn":"Compare ramp rates principle","text":"快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。","textEn":"Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients."},{"id":"a015-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「升溫斜率」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare ramp rates?","options":["快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"快速升溫會改變晶圓內外的暫態溫差。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Fast ramps change transient temperature gradients. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-10"],"title":"旋轉與均勻","titleEn":"Assess rotation averaging","objective":"完成「旋轉與均勻」的量測規劃，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess rotation averaging, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：旋轉與均勻。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess rotation averaging. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「旋轉與均勻」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess rotation averaging and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「旋轉與均勻」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for assess rotation averaging: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-11-k1","title":"旋轉與均勻的原理","titleEn":"Assess rotation averaging principle","text":"旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。","textEn":"Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations."},{"id":"a015-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「旋轉與均勻」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess rotation averaging?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"旋轉能平均方位誤差但不能消除所有徑向偏差。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Rotation averages angular errors but not all radial deviations. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}},{"id":"a015-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-11"],"title":"冷卻尾端","titleEn":"Include the cooling tail","objective":"完成「冷卻尾端」的工程驗收單，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for include the cooling tail, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：冷卻尾端。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Include the cooling tail. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Diffusion can continue during cooling. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Diffusion can continue during cooling. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「冷卻尾端」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for include the cooling tail and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「冷卻尾端」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for include the cooling tail: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-12-k1","title":"冷卻尾端的原理","titleEn":"Include the cooling tail principle","text":"降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。","textEn":"Diffusion can continue during cooling."},{"id":"a015-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","textEn":"Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「冷卻尾端」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating include the cooling tail?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Diffusion can continue during cooling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"降溫期間仍可能累積擴散。 高溫計將光輻射轉為溫度時需要發射率模型；表面堆疊不同會改變同一訊號的解釋。","explanationEn":"Diffusion can continue during cooling. Pyrometry converts radiance to temperature using emissivity; different surface stacks change interpretation of the same signal."}}]},{"id":"a015-stage03","order":3,"title":"電性與形貌","titleEn":"Electrical and structural outcomes","description":"在「電性與形貌」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for electrical and structural outcomes, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a015-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-12"],"title":"片電阻前後","titleEn":"Compare sheet resistance","objective":"完成「片電阻前後」的因果圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for compare sheet resistance, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：片電阻前後。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Compare sheet resistance. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「片電阻前後」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for compare sheet resistance and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「片電阻前後」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for compare sheet resistance: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-13-k1","title":"片電阻前後的原理","titleEn":"Compare sheet resistance principle","text":"片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。","textEn":"Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth."},{"id":"a015-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「片電阻前後」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating compare sheet resistance?","options":["片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"片電阻下降需與接面深度同時比較。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Reduced sheet resistance should be assessed with junction depth. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-13"],"title":"濃度輪廓展寬","titleEn":"Measure profile broadening","objective":"完成「濃度輪廓展寬」的對照表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for measure profile broadening, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：濃度輪廓展寬。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure profile broadening. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「濃度輪廓展寬」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure profile broadening and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「濃度輪廓展寬」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for measure profile broadening: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-14-k1","title":"濃度輪廓展寬的原理","titleEn":"Measure profile broadening principle","text":"較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。","textEn":"Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control."},{"id":"a015-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「濃度輪廓展寬」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure profile broadening?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"較深的尾端可能使短通道控制變差。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Deeper profile tails can degrade short-channel control. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-14"],"title":"接面漏電圖","titleEn":"Map junction leakage","objective":"完成「接面漏電圖」的敏感度草圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for map junction leakage, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接面漏電圖。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Map junction leakage. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「接面漏電圖」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for map junction leakage and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接面漏電圖」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for map junction leakage: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-15-k1","title":"接面漏電圖的原理","titleEn":"Map junction leakage principle","text":"漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。","textEn":"Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage."},{"id":"a015-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接面漏電圖」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating map junction leakage?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏電圖可揭示局部殘留損傷。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Leakage maps can reveal localized residual damage. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-15"],"title":"滑移線","titleEn":"Inspect slip lines","objective":"完成「滑移線」的故障判別表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect slip lines, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：滑移線。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect slip lines. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「滑移線」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect slip lines and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「滑移線」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect slip lines: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-16-k1","title":"滑移線的原理","titleEn":"Inspect slip lines principle","text":"熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。","textEn":"Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects."},{"id":"a015-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「滑移線」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect slip lines?","options":["熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱應力可能造成晶體塑性缺陷。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Thermal stress can generate crystalline slip defects. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-16"],"title":"翹曲回復","titleEn":"Measure bow evolution","objective":"完成「翹曲回復」的量測規劃，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for measure bow evolution, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：翹曲回復。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Measure bow evolution. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「翹曲回復」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for measure bow evolution and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「翹曲回復」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for measure bow evolution: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-17-k1","title":"翹曲回復的原理","titleEn":"Measure bow evolution principle","text":"退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。","textEn":"Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions."},{"id":"a015-v8-17-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「翹曲回復」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating measure bow evolution?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"退火前後形貌變化需使用一致支撐條件。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Before-after shape comparisons need consistent support conditions. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}},{"id":"a015-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-17"],"title":"圖案吸收差","titleEn":"Assess pattern-dependent absorption","objective":"完成「圖案吸收差」的工程驗收單，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for assess pattern-dependent absorption, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：圖案吸收差。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess pattern-dependent absorption. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「圖案吸收差」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess pattern-dependent absorption and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「圖案吸收差」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for assess pattern-dependent absorption: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-18-k1","title":"圖案吸收差的原理","titleEn":"Assess pattern-dependent absorption principle","text":"裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。","textEn":"Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity."},{"id":"a015-v8-18-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","textEn":"Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「圖案吸收差」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess pattern-dependent absorption?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"裸晶圓均勻性不能保證圖案晶圓均勻性。 活化改善可降低片電阻，但缺陷引起的接面漏電可能仍存在；兩者需以獨立結構量測。","explanationEn":"Blanket-wafer uniformity does not prove patterned-wafer uniformity. Activation can reduce sheet resistance while defect-induced junction leakage remains; measure both using independent structures."}}]},{"id":"a015-stage04","order":4,"title":"製程窗口","titleEn":"Process-window evidence","description":"在「製程窗口」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for process-window evidence, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a015-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-18"],"title":"峰值與停留權衡","titleEn":"Trade peak temperature against dwell","objective":"完成「峰值與停留權衡」的因果圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for trade peak temperature against dwell, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：峰值與停留權衡。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trade peak temperature against dwell. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「峰值與停留權衡」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trade peak temperature against dwell and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「峰值與停留權衡」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for trade peak temperature against dwell: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-19-k1","title":"峰值與停留權衡的原理","titleEn":"Trade peak temperature against dwell principle","text":"更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。","textEn":"Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks."},{"id":"a015-v8-19-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「峰值與停留權衡」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trade peak temperature against dwell?","options":["更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更短停留不能無條件抵銷更高峰值的所有效應。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Shorter dwell does not universally cancel all effects of higher peaks. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-19"],"title":"不確定度傳播","titleEn":"Propagate temperature uncertainty","objective":"完成「不確定度傳播」的對照表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for propagate temperature uncertainty, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：不確定度傳播。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Propagate temperature uncertainty. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「不確定度傳播」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for propagate temperature uncertainty and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「不確定度傳播」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for propagate temperature uncertainty: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-20-k1","title":"不確定度傳播的原理","titleEn":"Propagate temperature uncertainty principle","text":"小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。","textEn":"Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes."},{"id":"a015-v8-20-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「不確定度傳播」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating propagate temperature uncertainty?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"小溫度誤差可放大為擴散或活化差異。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Small temperature errors can amplify into diffusion or activation changes. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-20"],"title":"監控片轉移","titleEn":"Transfer monitor calibration","objective":"完成「監控片轉移」的敏感度草圖，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for transfer monitor calibration, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：監控片轉移。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Transfer monitor calibration. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「監控片轉移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for transfer monitor calibration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「監控片轉移」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for transfer monitor calibration: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-21-k1","title":"監控片轉移的原理","titleEn":"Transfer monitor calibration principle","text":"監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。","textEn":"Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers."},{"id":"a015-v8-21-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「監控片轉移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating transfer monitor calibration?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"監控片光學性質需與產品晶圓相容。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Monitor optical properties should represent product wafers. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-21"],"title":"批間漂移","titleEn":"Detect run-to-run drift","objective":"完成「批間漂移」的故障判別表，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for detect run-to-run drift, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：批間漂移。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Detect run-to-run drift. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「批間漂移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for detect run-to-run drift and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「批間漂移」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for detect run-to-run drift: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-22-k1","title":"批間漂移的原理","titleEn":"Detect run-to-run drift principle","text":"燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。","textEn":"Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift."},{"id":"a015-v8-22-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「批間漂移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating detect run-to-run drift?","options":["燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。","空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift.","Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"燈老化或腔體狀態變化可造成漸進漂移。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Lamp aging and chamber changes can create gradual drift. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-22"],"title":"跨模組交接","titleEn":"Handoff thermal constraints","objective":"完成「跨模組交接」的量測規劃，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for handoff thermal constraints, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：跨模組交接。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Handoff thermal constraints. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「跨模組交接」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for handoff thermal constraints and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「跨模組交接」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for handoff thermal constraints: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-23-k1","title":"跨模組交接的原理","titleEn":"Handoff thermal constraints principle","text":"閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。","textEn":"Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits."},{"id":"a015-v8-23-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「跨模組交接」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating handoff thermal constraints?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"閘介電層、接觸與應力層皆有各自熱限制。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Gate dielectrics, contacts and stress layers have distinct thermal limits. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}},{"id":"a015-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v8a-frontend"],"prerequisiteIds":["a015-v8-23"],"title":"退火窗口放行","titleEn":"Accept the annealing window","objective":"完成「退火窗口放行」的工程驗收單，把溫度時間軌跡、擴散、片電阻中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for accept the annealing window, connecting relevant limits in temperature-time history, diffusion and sheet resistance to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：退火窗口放行。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Accept the annealing window. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。 應回到「退火窗口放行」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity. Revisit assumptions and sampling for accept the annealing window and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「退火窗口放行」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for accept the annealing window: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a015-v8-24-k1","title":"退火窗口放行的原理","titleEn":"Accept the annealing window principle","text":"活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。","textEn":"Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria."},{"id":"a015-v8-24-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","textEn":"The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「退火窗口放行」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating accept the annealing window?","options":["空載均溫就證明滿載各片均勻。","相同雷射能量必定產生相同熱峰值。","活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。"],"optionsEn":["Empty-furnace uniformity proves loaded-wafer uniformity.","Equal laser energy must produce equal thermal peaks.","Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria."],"answer":2,"explanation":"活化、擴散、漏電及結構損傷需共同滿足。 退火窗口是活化、擴散及材料耐受的交集，不能只選片電阻最低的條件當作整合最佳值。","explanationEn":"Activation, diffusion, leakage and structural damage must all meet criteria. The anneal window intersects activation, diffusion and material survival; minimum sheet resistance alone is not an integrated optimum."}}]}],"subcategory":"feol","subcategoryTitle":"前段材料與接面","subcategoryTitleEn":"FEOL materials and junctions"},{"id":"a016","title":"雷射尖峰退火","titleEn":"Laser spike annealing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以 4 階段、24 個工程工作包拆解光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收，完成圖解、對照、敏感度分析、故障判別、量測規劃與驗收。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 work packages explore beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption through diagrams, comparisons, sensitivity studies, fault diagnosis, measurement plans and acceptance reviews.","sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"依公開原理編寫的雙語概念實作課；每步交付可審查的工程證據。24 步是學習拆解，不代表晶圓廠的完整配方。自行設定的數值須標為假設。題目不含可直接操作的化學混配、設備設定或量產公差；照片與外部影片為代表媒體，不是假稱每步實拍。","scopeEn":"Bilingual conceptual exercises based on public principles, with reviewable evidence at each step. The 24 steps are a learning decomposition, not a complete fab recipe. Chosen numerical inputs must be labeled hypothetical. No directly operable chemical mixtures, equipment settings or production tolerances are supplied. Photos and external videos are representative media, not claimed as recordings of every step.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["雷射熱歷程","光束與掃描","局部反應","圖案相容性"],"labelsEn":["Laser thermal history","Beam and scanning","Localized response","Pattern compatibility"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a016-stage01","order":1,"title":"雷射熱歷程","titleEn":"Laser thermal history","description":"在「雷射熱歷程」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for laser thermal history, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a016-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"毫秒與奈秒","titleEn":"Separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes","objective":"完成「毫秒與奈秒」的因果圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：毫秒與奈秒。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「毫秒與奈秒」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「毫秒與奈秒」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-01-k1","title":"毫秒與奈秒的原理","titleEn":"Separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes principle","text":"不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。","textEn":"Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process."},{"id":"a016-v8-01-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「毫秒與奈秒」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate millisecond and nanosecond regimes?","options":["不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同脈衝時間不能視為同一熱處理。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Different pulse durations cannot be treated as the same thermal process. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-01"],"title":"光吸收深度","titleEn":"Assess optical penetration","objective":"完成「光吸收深度」的對照表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess optical penetration, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：光吸收深度。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess optical penetration. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「光吸收深度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess optical penetration and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「光吸收深度」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess optical penetration: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-02-k1","title":"光吸收深度的原理","titleEn":"Assess optical penetration principle","text":"光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。","textEn":"Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth."},{"id":"a016-v8-02-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「光吸收深度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess optical penetration?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光學吸收與熱擴散共同決定加熱深度。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Optical absorption and thermal diffusion jointly set heated depth. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-02"],"title":"熱擴散尺度","titleEn":"Estimate thermal diffusion length","objective":"完成「熱擴散尺度」的敏感度草圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for estimate thermal diffusion length, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱擴散尺度。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Estimate thermal diffusion length. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「熱擴散尺度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for estimate thermal diffusion length and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱擴散尺度」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for estimate thermal diffusion length: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-03-k1","title":"熱擴散尺度的原理","titleEn":"Estimate thermal diffusion length principle","text":"熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time."},{"id":"a016-v8-03-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱擴散尺度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating estimate thermal diffusion length?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱擴散長度隨時間平方根改變。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales with the square root of time. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-03"],"title":"峰值與積分能量","titleEn":"Separate peak and integrated energy","objective":"完成「峰值與積分能量」的故障判別表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for separate peak and integrated energy, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：峰值與積分能量。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Separate peak and integrated energy. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「峰值與積分能量」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for separate peak and integrated energy and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「峰值與積分能量」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for separate peak and integrated energy: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-04-k1","title":"峰值與積分能量的原理","titleEn":"Separate peak and integrated energy principle","text":"相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。","textEn":"Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures."},{"id":"a016-v8-04-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「峰值與積分能量」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating separate peak and integrated energy?","options":["相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。","峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures.","Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同能量可能有不同峰值溫度。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Equal energy can produce different peak temperatures. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-04"],"title":"熔融與非熔融","titleEn":"Distinguish melting regimes","objective":"完成「熔融與非熔融」的量測規劃，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for distinguish melting regimes, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熔融與非熔融。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Distinguish melting regimes. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「熔融與非熔融」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for distinguish melting regimes and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熔融與非熔融」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for distinguish melting regimes: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-05-k1","title":"熔融與非熔融的原理","titleEn":"Distinguish melting regimes principle","text":"是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。","textEn":"Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms."},{"id":"a016-v8-05-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熔融與非熔融」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating distinguish melting regimes?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"是否熔融會改變再結晶及摻雜重分布機制。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Melting changes recrystallization and dopant redistribution mechanisms. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}},{"id":"a016-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-05"],"title":"熱敏感下層","titleEn":"Identify sensitive underlying layers","objective":"完成「熱敏感下層」的工程驗收單，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for identify sensitive underlying layers, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：熱敏感下層。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Identify sensitive underlying layers. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。 應回到「熱敏感下層」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets. Revisit assumptions and sampling for identify sensitive underlying layers and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「熱敏感下層」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for identify sensitive underlying layers: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-06-k1","title":"熱敏感下層的原理","titleEn":"Identify sensitive underlying layers principle","text":"表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。","textEn":"Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment."},{"id":"a016-v8-06-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","textEn":"Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「熱敏感下層」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating identify sensitive underlying layers?","options":["峰值溫度相同便有相同擴散預算。","化學摻雜濃度就是活化載子濃度。","表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peak temperatures imply equal diffusion budgets.","Chemical dopant concentration equals active carrier concentration.","Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面短暫加熱仍需檢查下層最高溫度。 熱擴散尺度約與時間平方根成正比；縮短熱脈衝可減少深部受熱，但表面溫度仍需量測。","explanationEn":"Brief surface heating still requires subsurface peak-temperature assessment. Thermal diffusion length scales roughly with square-root time; shorter pulses reduce deep heating but still require surface thermometry."}}]},{"id":"a016-stage02","order":2,"title":"光束與掃描","titleEn":"Beam and scanning","description":"在「光束與掃描」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for beam and scanning, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a016-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-06"],"title":"光斑強度剖面","titleEn":"Read the beam profile","objective":"完成「光斑強度剖面」的因果圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for read the beam profile, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：光斑強度剖面。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Read the beam profile. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Mean power does not describe local beam intensity. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Mean power does not describe local beam intensity. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「光斑強度剖面」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for read the beam profile and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「光斑強度剖面」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for read the beam profile: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-07-k1","title":"光斑強度剖面的原理","titleEn":"Read the beam profile principle","text":"平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。","textEn":"Mean power does not describe local beam intensity."},{"id":"a016-v8-07-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「光斑強度剖面」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating read the beam profile?","options":["平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Mean power does not describe local beam intensity.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均功率不能代表光斑內局部強度。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Mean power does not describe local beam intensity. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-07"],"title":"掃描速度","titleEn":"Relate scan speed and dwell","objective":"完成「掃描速度」的對照表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for relate scan speed and dwell, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：掃描速度。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。 自訂掃描幾何：光斑寬 0.1 mm、掃速 100 mm/s；求單點名義停留時間，再把掃速加倍，並列出需另外處理的重疊與光斑非均勻。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Relate scan speed and dwell. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs. Hypothetical scan: beam width 0.1 mm and speed 100 mm/s. Compute nominal dwell, double the speed, and list overlap and beam nonuniformity effects requiring separate treatment.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「掃描速度」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for relate scan speed and dwell and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「掃描速度」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。 同時交付算例的中間步驟或比較圖，並標示假設與模型限制。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for relate scan speed and dwell: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder. Also submit intermediate calculations or comparison diagrams with assumptions and model limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-08-k1","title":"掃描速度的原理","titleEn":"Relate scan speed and dwell principle","text":"固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。","textEn":"With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell."},{"id":"a016-v8-08-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「掃描速度」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating relate scan speed and dwell?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"固定光斑寬度下掃速決定局部暴露時間。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"With fixed beam width, scan speed determines local dwell. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-08"],"title":"重疊帶","titleEn":"Assess scan overlap","objective":"完成「重疊帶」的敏感度草圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for assess scan overlap, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：重疊帶。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess scan overlap. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「重疊帶」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess scan overlap and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「重疊帶」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for assess scan overlap: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-09-k1","title":"重疊帶的原理","titleEn":"Assess scan overlap principle","text":"相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。","textEn":"Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure."},{"id":"a016-v8-09-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「重疊帶」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess scan overlap?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相鄰掃描重疊區可能接受不同累計暴露。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Adjacent scan overlaps can receive different cumulative exposure. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-09"],"title":"邊緣轉向","titleEn":"Inspect scan turnarounds","objective":"完成「邊緣轉向」的故障判別表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect scan turnarounds, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：邊緣轉向。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect scan turnarounds. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「邊緣轉向」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect scan turnarounds and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「邊緣轉向」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect scan turnarounds: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-10-k1","title":"邊緣轉向的原理","titleEn":"Inspect scan turnarounds principle","text":"掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。","textEn":"Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area."},{"id":"a016-v8-10-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「邊緣轉向」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect scan turnarounds?","options":["掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。","片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area.","Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"掃描加減速區應與有效晶圓區分開。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Acceleration regions must be distinguished from the usable wafer area. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-10"],"title":"溫度回授延遲","titleEn":"Account for thermal-feedback delay","objective":"完成「溫度回授延遲」的量測規劃，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for account for thermal-feedback delay, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：溫度回授延遲。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Account for thermal-feedback delay. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「溫度回授延遲」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for account for thermal-feedback delay and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「溫度回授延遲」量測規劃：提供採樣座標、量測單位、對照與不確定度來源。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan for account for thermal-feedback delay: Provide sampling coordinates, units, controls and uncertainty sources.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-11-k1","title":"溫度回授延遲的原理","titleEn":"Account for thermal-feedback delay principle","text":"感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。","textEn":"Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks."},{"id":"a016-v8-11-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「溫度回授延遲」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating account for thermal-feedback delay?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature."],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測延遲可能錯過短暫溫度峰值。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Sensor delay can miss short temperature peaks. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}},{"id":"a016-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-11"],"title":"功率漂移","titleEn":"Track laser-power drift","objective":"完成「功率漂移」的工程驗收單，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a engineering acceptance sheet for track laser-power drift, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：功率漂移。整合本步及本階段先前證據；提出兩項彼此不同的接受條件；再列一個會讓你暫緩放行的結果及下一個確認動作。判讀依據：校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Track laser-power drift. Combine this step with earlier stage evidence; propose two independent acceptance criteria; name one hold condition and the next confirming action. Interpretation: Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。 應回到「功率漂移」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction. Revisit assumptions and sampling for track laser-power drift and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「功率漂移」工程驗收單：驗收單需有原理、兩項證據、保留疑問及前後模組交接。","checkEn":"Submit the engineering acceptance sheet for track laser-power drift: The sheet needs the principle, two evidence items, open questions and module handoff.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-12-k1","title":"功率漂移的原理","titleEn":"Track laser-power drift principle","text":"校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。","textEn":"Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions."},{"id":"a016-v8-12-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","textEn":"For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「功率漂移」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating track laser-power drift?","options":["片電阻下降就證明接面完全無損傷。","爐壁設定溫度等於晶圓瞬時溫度。","校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。"],"optionsEn":["Lower sheet resistance proves a damage-free junction.","Wall setpoint equals instantaneous wafer temperature.","Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"校準與實際處理需使用同一光路狀態。 固定光斑寬度時，停留時間約為寬度除以掃速；重疊區的累積歷程還需把相鄰掃描相加。","explanationEn":"Calibration and processing need consistent optical-path conditions. For a fixed beam width, dwell is roughly width divided by speed; overlap history also includes adjacent scans."}}]},{"id":"a016-stage03","order":3,"title":"局部反應","titleEn":"Localized response","description":"在「局部反應」建立六項互補證據，逐一檢查材料、幾何、物理機制與適用限制。","descriptionEn":"Build six complementary evidence items for localized response, checking materials, geometry, mechanisms and validity limits.","steps":[{"id":"a016-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-12"],"title":"摻雜活化","titleEn":"Evaluate dopant activation","objective":"完成「摻雜活化」的因果圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a causal diagram for evaluate dopant activation, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：摻雜活化。畫一張含作用前後狀態的原創圖；以箭頭標出本步原理中的因果關係；圈出一項仍需量測的未知量。判讀依據：短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Evaluate dopant activation. Draw an original before/after diagram; mark the causal relationship in this step; circle one quantity still requiring measurement. Interpretation: Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「摻雜活化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for evaluate dopant activation and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「摻雜活化」因果圖：圖中要有邊界、輸入、輸出與一項不能僅由圖決定的量。","checkEn":"Submit the causal diagram for evaluate dopant activation: Show boundaries, inputs, outputs and one quantity that the diagram alone cannot determine.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-13-k1","title":"摻雜活化的原理","titleEn":"Evaluate dopant activation principle","text":"短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。","textEn":"Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion."},{"id":"a016-v8-13-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「摻雜活化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating evaluate dopant activation?","options":["短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"短熱歷程可改變活化與擴散的相對程度。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Short thermal histories change the balance between activation and diffusion. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}},{"id":"a016-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-13"],"title":"接觸電阻改善","titleEn":"Assess contact-resistance change","objective":"完成「接觸電阻改善」的對照表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a controlled comparison for assess contact-resistance change, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：接觸電阻改善。建立兩個只改一項條件的假想案例；分開記錄可觀察差異與推測原因；說明如何用本步原理區分兩者。判讀依據：總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess contact-resistance change. Create two hypothetical cases differing in one condition; separate observations from proposed causes; use this step’s principle to distinguish them. Interpretation: Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「接觸電阻改善」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for assess contact-resistance change and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「接觸電阻改善」對照表：交出兩案例、固定條件、預期差異及一項可能混淆因素。","checkEn":"Submit the controlled comparison for assess contact-resistance change: Submit both cases, fixed conditions, predicted difference and one confounder.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-14-k1","title":"接觸電阻改善的原理","titleEn":"Assess contact-resistance change principle","text":"總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。","textEn":"Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface."},{"id":"a016-v8-14-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「接觸電阻改善」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating assess contact-resistance change?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"總串聯電阻下降不能自動歸因於接觸界面。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Lower total series resistance cannot automatically be attributed to the contact interface. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}},{"id":"a016-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-14"],"title":"再結晶前緣","titleEn":"Trace recrystallization fronts","objective":"完成「再結晶前緣」的敏感度草圖，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a sensitivity sketch for trace recrystallization fronts, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：再結晶前緣。選出本步的一項輸入及一項輸出；以自訂低、中、高三點畫趨勢；逐點標註假設，並寫出趨勢可能失效的條件。判讀依據：結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Trace recrystallization fronts. Select one input and output for this step; sketch a hypothetical low/mid/high trend; label assumptions and state when the trend may fail. Interpretation: Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「再結晶前緣」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for trace recrystallization fronts and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「再結晶前緣」敏感度草圖：圖須有變數、單位或無因次定義、三個假設點及適用範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the sensitivity sketch for trace recrystallization fronts: Include variables, units or dimensionless definitions, three hypothetical points and validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-15-k1","title":"再結晶前緣的原理","titleEn":"Trace recrystallization fronts principle","text":"結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。","textEn":"Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality."},{"id":"a016-v8-15-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「再結晶前緣」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating trace recrystallization fronts?","options":["降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。","結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。"],"optionsEn":["No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity.","Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality."],"answer":2,"explanation":"結晶前緣與缺陷位置共同影響最終品質。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Recrystallization fronts and defect positions jointly affect final quality. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}},{"id":"a016-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-15"],"title":"表面粗糙化","titleEn":"Inspect surface roughening","objective":"完成「表面粗糙化」的故障判別表，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a fault-discrimination table for inspect surface roughening, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：表面粗糙化。假設本步預期結果未出現；提出兩個不同機制；為各機制選一個能支持或否定的觀察，避免只重複同一量測。判讀依據：電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Inspect surface roughening. Assume the expected result fails; propose two distinct mechanisms; choose an observation that supports or rejects each rather than repeating one measurement. Interpretation: Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。」；若證據不足，標記尚未確定並寫出缺少的量測。","observationEn":"Check whether the evidence supports: Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation. If insufficient, mark the conclusion unresolved and name the missing measurement.","failure":"常見錯判：降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。 應回到「表面粗糙化」的假設與採樣範圍，補足能區分機制的證據。","failureEn":"Common misinterpretation: No diffusion can occur during cooling. Revisit assumptions and sampling for inspect surface roughening and add discriminating evidence.","check":"交付「表面粗糙化」故障判別表：至少列出兩個假說、各自的辨別證據及先檢查順序。","checkEn":"Submit the fault-discrimination table for inspect surface roughening: List two hypotheses, discriminating evidence for each and a check order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a016-v8-16-k1","title":"表面粗糙化的原理","titleEn":"Inspect surface roughening principle","text":"電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。","textEn":"Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation."},{"id":"a016-v8-16-k2","title":"本階段的機制與工程權衡","titleEn":"Stage mechanisms and engineering tradeoffs","text":"吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","textEn":"Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}],"quiz":{"question":"評估「表面粗糙化」時，哪項敘述可以採用？","questionEn":"Which statement is valid when evaluating inspect surface roughening?","options":["電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。","降溫期間不可能再發生擴散。","所有光學表面可共用不變發射率。"],"optionsEn":["Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation.","No diffusion can occur during cooling.","Every optical surface shares one constant emissivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電性改善也可能伴隨表面形貌劣化。 吸收能量轉為溫升要考慮熱容量、熱擴散與可能相變，因此入射能量不能直接當作局部最高溫。","explanationEn":"Electrical improvement can coexist with surface degradation. Temperature rise depends on heat capacity, diffusion and possible phase changes; incident energy is not local peak temperature."}},{"id":"a016-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8a-laser","v8a-rtp","v8a-implant"],"prerequisiteIds":["a016-v8-16"],"title":"應力尖峰","titleEn":"Assess transient stress","objective":"完成「應力尖峰」的量測規劃，把光斑掃描、局部熱峰、圖案吸收中的相關限制連到可觀察證據。","objectiveEn":"Complete a measurement plan for assess transient stress, connecting relevant limits in beam scanning, local thermal peaks and patterned absorption to observable evidence.","instruction":"本步問題：應力尖峰。針對本步定義待測量及採樣位置；列出解析度、背景與重複性；設計一個見證或空白，並說明檢出限如何限制結論。判讀依據：局部急熱可產生與平均溫升不同的應力峰值。引用列出的原始資料；若使用數值，清楚標成自訂教學假設。","instructionEn":"Question for this step: Assess transient stress. Define the measurand and sampling locations; list resolution, background and repeatability; design a witness or blank and explain detection-limit constraints. Interpretation: Localized rapid heating can create stress peaks unlike average warming. Cite the listed primary material; label any chosen numbers as hypothetical educational inputs.","observation":"檢查結果是否能支持「局部急熱可產生與平均溫升不同的應力峰值。」；若證據不足，標記尚未�